window.NEXA_DOCS = {"chapters": [{"slug": "getting-started", "title": "Getting Started", "group": "Start Here", "source": "docs/getting-started.md", "html": "<h1 id=\"getting-started-core-mental-model\">Getting Started &amp; Core Mental Model</h1>\n<p>Welcome to <strong>nexa</strong>! Whether you have built desktop UIs with Tkinter, PyQt, Dear ImGui, or React—or this is your very first Python GUI library—this guide walks you from zero to building fast, polished desktop tools in minutes.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"1-installation-requirements\">1. Installation &amp; Requirements</h2>\n<p>Install <code>nexa</code> from the repository root:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>bash</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install .</code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"what-you-need-and-what-you-don-t-need\">What you need (and what you <em>don&#x27;t</em> need)</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Python 3.9+</strong> (zero third-party runtime Python packages—pure standard library).</li><li><strong>Any C99 compiler</strong> when installing from source (<code>gcc</code> or <code>clang</code> on Linux/macOS, MSVC <code>cl</code> or MinGW <code>gcc</code> on Windows).</li><li>**No <code>python3-dev</code> headers, no CMake, and no <code>libx11-dev</code> packages required!** On Linux, <code>nexa</code> dynamically loads <code>libX11.so.6</code> via <code>dlopen</code> at runtime, and automatically falls back to its built-in multi-threaded CPU <code>SoftwareRenderer</code> when running on headless servers or CI.</li></ul>\n<p>To manually rebuild the native shared library (<code>libnexa_cui.so</code> / <code>.dylib</code> / <code>.dll</code>) at any time:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>bash</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python3 -m nexa.build</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"2-your-first-15-line-window\">2. Your First 15-Line Window</h2>\n<p>Create a file named <code>first_app.py</code> and run <code>python3 first_app.py</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\ncount = <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>\nname = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;world&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">global</span> count, name\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">14</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n        ui.heading(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Hello, {name or &#x27;stranger&#x27;}!&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>)\n        name = ui.input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;name_field&quot;</span>, name, label=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Your name&quot;</span>, clearable=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>)\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>, align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Increment&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PLUS</span>):\n                count += <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>\n            ui.badge(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Clicked {count}x&quot;</span>, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACCENT</span>)\n\nui.run(draw, title=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;My First nexa Window&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">520</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">300</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"headless-screenshot-mode-servers-containers-ci\">Headless Screenshot Mode (Servers, Containers &amp; CI)</h3>\n<p>Don&#x27;t have a display attached right now? Every <code>nexa</code> app can render pixel-identical frames off-screen and save a PNG screenshot via environment variables:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>bash</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>NEXA_HEADLESS=1 CUI_SCREENSHOT=preview.png CUI_SCREENSHOT_FRAMES=10 python3 first_app.py</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"3-how-nexa-thinks-value-returning-immediate-mode\">3. How <code>nexa</code> Thinks: Value-Returning Immediate Mode</h2>\n<p>Traditional retained-mode toolkits (Tkinter, Qt, GTK) force you to keep <strong>two copies of your state</strong> synchronized:</p>\n<ol><li>Your Python data (<code>user.name</code>), and</li><li>Hidden state inside widget objects (<code>name_entry.setText(...)</code>, <code>on_text_changed</code> callbacks, signals/slots).</li></ol>\n<p><code>nexa</code> uses an <strong>event-driven, value-returning immediate-mode</strong> architecture:</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Your Python variables are the single source of truth.</strong> You pass the current value into a widget, and the widget returns the new value:</li></ol>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>   <span class=\"tok-com\"># Text input: str -&gt; str</span>\n   query = ui.search(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;q&quot;</span>, query, placeholder=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Filter...&quot;</span>)\n\n   <span class=\"tok-com\"># Switch / Checkbox: bool -&gt; bool</span>\n   dark = ui.switch(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Dark mode&quot;</span>, dark)\n\n   <span class=\"tok-com\"># Slider: float -&gt; float</span>\n   volume = ui.slider(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Volume&quot;</span>, volume, <span class=\"tok-num\">0.0</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">1.0</span>, show_value=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>)\n\n   <span class=\"tok-com\"># Button: returns True on the exact frame it was clicked!</span>\n   <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Save&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>):\n       save_to_disk()</code></pre></div>\n<ol><li><strong>UI is just plain Python control flow.</strong> Want to hide an input unless <code>advanced</code> is enabled? Use a regular <code>if</code>:</li></ol>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>   advanced = ui.checkbox(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Show advanced options&quot;</span>, advanced)\n   <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> advanced:\n       port = int(ui.number(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;port&quot;</span>, port, <span class=\"tok-num\">1024</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">65535</span>, step=<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>, decimals=<span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>))</code></pre></div>\n<p>Want to render a list of items? Use a regular <code>for</code> loop!</p>\n<ol><li><strong>0% CPU when idle, 60–120 fps spring physics when active.</strong> Unlike game-engine immediate-mode GUIs that burn 100% of a core spinning in <code>while True</code>, <code>nexa</code> blocks inside the OS event loop (<code>select</code> / <code>GetMessageW</code> / <code>NSApp</code>) consuming <strong>0% CPU</strong> until mouse/keyboard input arrives, a spring animation is in flight, or a background thread calls <code>app.wake()</code>.</li></ol>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"4-widget-identity-id-id-scope\">4. Widget Identity (<code>id</code> &amp; <code>id_scope</code>)</h2>\n<p>To animate hover states, track keyboard focus, and remember scroll offsets across frames, <code>nexa</code> hashes an ID string for every interactive widget:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Controls with a unique key parameter</strong> (<code>input(&quot;email&quot;, ...)</code>, <code>tabs(&quot;main_tabs&quot;, ...)</code>, <code>slider(&quot;Volume&quot;, ...)</code>) hash that first string argument.</li><li><strong>Buttons &amp; toggles</strong> (<code>button(&quot;Save&quot;)</code>, <code>checkbox(&quot;Agree&quot;, ...)</code>) hash their label string.</li><li>**<code>label##hidden_id</code> syntax**: Just like Dear ImGui / CUI, everything from <code>##</code> onward contributes to the ID hash <em>without</em> being drawn on screen!<ul><li><code>&quot;Delete##row_1&quot;</code> and <code>&quot;Delete##row_2&quot;</code> both display **<code>Delete</code>**, while having completely distinct IDs.</li><li><code>&quot;##search&quot;</code> has an empty visible label and hashes <code>&quot;##search&quot;</code>.</li></ul></li><li>**Loops &amp; Reusable Blocks (<code>id_scope</code>)**: Whenever you render widgets inside a <code>for</code> loop, wrap each iteration in <code>with ui.id_scope(item_id):</code> (or <code>with ctx.id_scope(i):</code>) so every iteration gets its own isolated ID namespace:</li></ul>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> idx, task <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> enumerate(tasks):\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.id_scope(idx):\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">8</span>, align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>):\n            task[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;done&quot;</span>] = ui.checkbox(task[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>], task[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;done&quot;</span>])\n            ui.spacer()\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Delete&quot;</span>, size=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ControlSize</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SM</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GHOST</span>):\n                tasks.pop(idx)\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">break</span></code></pre></div>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Tip:</strong> When using the OOP API (<code>ui.Component</code>), <code>nexa</code> pushes <code>component.key</code> onto the ID stack <strong>automatically</strong>—you don&#x27;t even need manual <code>id_scope</code> calls between component instances!</p></blockquote>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"5-unconditional-vs-conditional-with-scopes\">5. Unconditional vs. Conditional <code>with</code> Scopes</h2>\n<p><code>nexa</code> uses Python <code>with</code> statements so you can never forget a <code>*_end()</code> call. There are two kinds of scopes:</p>\n<h3 id=\"a-unconditional-layout-scopes-always-render-children\">A. Unconditional Layout Scopes (always render children)</h3>\n<p>Containers that always open and close cleanly:</p>\n<ul><li><code>box</code>, <code>row</code>, <code>column</code>, <code>stack</code>, <code>grid</code>, <code>card</code>, <code>scroll</code>, <code>split</code></li><li><code>id_scope</code>, <code>disabled_scope</code>, <code>clip_scope</code></li><li><code>button_group</code>, <code>swipe_item</code>, <code>spotlight</code>, <code>dock</code>, <code>carousel</code>, <code>card_stack</code>, <code>kanban</code>, <code>virtual_list</code>, <code>reorder</code></li><li><code>menu_bar</code>, <code>toolbar</code>, <code>status_bar</code>, <code>dialog_footer</code></li></ul>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">20</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>):\n    ui.heading(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Always rendered&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">3</span>)\n    ui.secondary(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Card body&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"b-conditional-scopes-check-if-scope-before-rendering-children\">B. Conditional Scopes (check <code>if scope:</code> before rendering children!)</h3>\n<p>Overlays, disclosures, menus, and popups only build their children when open or visible. Always bind <code>as s:</code> and check <code>if s:</code>:</p>\n<ul><li>Overlays &amp; Menus: <code>dialog</code>, <code>sheet</code>, <code>popover</code>, <code>hover_card</code>, <code>menu</code>, <code>context_menu</code>, <code>user_menu</code>, <code>menu_bar_menu</code></li><li>Disclosures &amp; Trees: <code>accordion</code>, <code>expandable_card</code>, <code>tree</code>, <code>reasoning</code></li><li>Structured Views: <code>table</code>, <code>data_grid</code>, <code>inspector</code>, <code>node_editor</code></li></ul>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.dialog(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Confirm Reset&quot;</span>, is_open, description=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Reset all settings to defaults?&quot;</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> dlg:\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> dlg:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.dialog_footer():\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Cancel&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GHOST</span>):\n                dlg.open = <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Reset&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DANGER</span>):\n                reset_all()\n                dlg.open = <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>\nis_open = dlg.open  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Also catches Escape key or backdrop click!</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"6-inspecting-transitions-changed-submitted-focused-blurred-rects\">6. Inspecting Transitions (<code>changed</code>, <code>submitted</code>, <code>focused</code>, <code>blurred</code>) &amp; Rects</h2>\n<p>Even though widgets return updated values directly, you often want to know <em>how</em> a widget transitioned on the current frame (for example, running a search when the user presses <strong>Enter</strong> inside <code>ui.input</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query = ui.input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;cmd&quot;</span>, query, placeholder=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Type command and press Enter...&quot;</span>)\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.changed():\n    print(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Text edited this frame:&quot;</span>, query)\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.submitted():\n    run_command(query)  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Fired when Enter is pressed!</span>\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.focused():\n    print(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Input just gained focus&quot;</span>)\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.blurred():\n    print(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Input just lost focus&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<p>On an explicit <code>ctx: ui.UI</code> instance, these are properties: <code>ctx.changed</code>, <code>ctx.submitted</code>, <code>ctx.focused</code>, <code>ctx.blurred</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"widget-hit-rectangles-last-id-last-rect-get-rect\">Widget Hit Rectangles (<code>last_id</code>, <code>last_rect</code>, <code>get_rect</code>)</h3>\n<p>Because CUI computes flexbox/grid layout in a single pass inside <code>end_frame()</code>:</p>\n<ul><li>During <code>draw()</code>, <code>ctx.last_id</code> gives the <code>uint32</code> ID of the widget you just emitted, and <code>ctx.last_rect</code> returns its cached <code>Rect(x, y, w, h)</code> from the previous frame.</li><li>Immediately after <code>end_frame()</code>, <code>ctx.get_rect(widget_id)</code> returns the exact newly computed <code>Rect(x, y, w, h)</code> for the frame that just finished.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next Steps</h2>\n<p>Choose the coding style you want to learn first (most developers read <strong>both</strong>, because they share the exact same widget names and compose together!):</p>\n<ol><li><strong><a href=\"#tutorial-functional\" data-doc-link=\"tutorial-functional\">Functional &amp; Procedural Tutorial →</a></strong> — Closures, explicit <code>ctx: ui.UI</code> helper functions, flexbox/grid layouts, forms, shortcuts, and manual frame loops.</li><li><strong><a href=\"#tutorial-oop\" data-doc-link=\"tutorial-oop\">Object-Oriented (OOP) Tutorial →</a></strong> — <code>Application</code>, auto-scoped <code>Component</code> classes, multi-screen <code>Router</code> &amp; <code>View</code>, and reactive <code>Store</code>.</li><li><strong><a href=\"#theming-and-styling\" data-doc-link=\"theming-and-styling\">Theming, Accents, Tones &amp; Icons →</a></strong> — All 8 real <code>Accent</code> presets, 9 <code>Tone</code>s, custom OKLCH tokens, fonts, and 168 icons.</li></ol>", "toc": [{"title": "1. Installation & Requirements", "id": "1-installation-requirements"}, {"title": "2. Your First 15-Line Window", "id": "2-your-first-15-line-window"}, {"title": "3. How nexa Thinks: Value-Returning Immediate Mode", "id": "3-how-nexa-thinks-value-returning-immediate-mode"}, {"title": "4. Widget Identity (id & id_scope)", "id": "4-widget-identity-id-id-scope"}, {"title": "5. Unconditional vs. Conditional with Scopes", "id": "5-unconditional-vs-conditional-with-scopes"}, {"title": "6. Inspecting Transitions (changed, submitted, focused, blurred) & Rects", "id": "6-inspecting-transitions-changed-submitted-focused-blurred-rects"}, {"title": "Next Steps", "id": "next-steps"}]}, {"slug": "tutorial-functional", "title": "Functional & Procedural", "group": "Tutorials", "source": "docs/tutorial-functional.md", "html": "<h1 id=\"tutorial-functional-procedural-coding\">Tutorial: Functional &amp; Procedural Coding</h1>\n<p><code>nexa</code> lets you write clean, Pythonic desktop applications <strong>without a single class</strong> when you want speed, simplicity, and direct data flow.</p>\n<p>In fact, <code>nexa</code> supports <strong>two closely related non-OOP styles</strong>:</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Top-Level Functional Style</strong> (<code>import nexa as ui</code> + <code>ui.heading(...)</code>, <code>ui.button(...)</code>): Uses a lightweight <code>contextvars.ContextVar</code> under the hood so you don&#x27;t even pass a context parameter around. Ideal for scripts, prototypes, and single-file tools.</li><li><strong>Explicit Procedural Style</strong> (<code>def render_sidebar(ctx: ui.UI, state: dict)</code>): Passes <code>ctx: ui.UI</code> explicitly as the first argument to plain Python functions. Ideal for larger procedural codebases, multi-window tools, and unit-tested UI modules.</li></ol>\n<p>Let&#x27;s master both step by step!</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-1-top-level-functional-basics\">Lesson 1: Top-Level Functional Basics</h2>\n<p>With <code>ui.run(draw)</code>, your <code>draw</code> function takes <strong>0 arguments</strong> (or 1 <code>ctx: ui.UI</code> argument—<code>ui.run</code> inspects its signature automatically!).</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> main() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    celsius = <span class=\"tok-num\">22.0</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">nonlocal</span> celsius\n        fahrenheit = celsius * <span class=\"tok-num\">9.0</span> / <span class=\"tok-num\">5.0</span> + <span class=\"tok-num\">32.0</span>\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.column(\n            width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">28</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>,\n            align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>, justify=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Justify</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>,\n        ):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.card(width=<span class=\"tok-num\">380</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">14</span>):\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.row(align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>):\n                    ui.heading(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Thermostat&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)\n                    ui.spacer()\n                    ui.theme_toggle()\n\n                celsius = ui.slider(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Temperature&quot;</span>, celsius, -<span class=\"tok-num\">10.0</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">45.0</span>, step=<span class=\"tok-num\">0.5</span>, show_value=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>, format=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;%.1f °C&quot;</span>)\n                ui.metric(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Fahrenheit&quot;</span>, f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;{fahrenheit:.1f} °F&quot;</span>, delta=celsius - <span class=\"tok-num\">20.0</span>)\n\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">8</span>):\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Eco (19 °C)&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CHECK</span>):\n                        celsius = <span class=\"tok-num\">19.0</span>\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ui.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Comfort (22 °C)&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>):\n                        celsius = <span class=\"tok-num\">22.0</span>\n\n    ui.run(draw, title=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Thermostat&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">500</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">380</span>, accent=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CORAL</span>)\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    main()</code></pre></div>\n<p>Wait—notice how clean <code>nonlocal celsius</code> is for 1–3 variables. What when you have 10+ state fields? In procedural Python, put your state in a plain <code>dict</code> (or custom state object) so you never need <code>global</code> or <code>nonlocal</code>!</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-2-mastering-flexbox-sizing-grids\">Lesson 2: Mastering Flexbox, Sizing &amp; Grids</h2>\n<p>Every container in <code>nexa</code> (<code>box</code>, <code>row</code>, <code>column</code>, <code>stack</code>, <code>grid</code>, <code>card</code>, <code>scroll</code>) uses the same single-pass constraint layout system.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-5-sizing-primitives\">The 5 Sizing Primitives</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Sizing Spec</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ui.FIT</code> *(or <code>None</code>)*</td><td>Shrink-wrap to fit child content</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.FILL</code></td><td>Stretch to 100% of available parent space</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.GROW(weight)</code></td><td>Flex-grow proportionally along a <code>row</code> or <code>column</code> (<code>GROW(2)</code> takes 2x space of <code>GROW(1)</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>240</code> or <code>ui.PX(240)</code></td><td>Exact logical pixel size (automatically scaled by HiDPI <code>ctx.scale</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.PCT(50)</code></td><td>Percentage (<code>0..100</code>) of parent dimension</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3 id=\"classic-desktop-shell-recipe-sidebar-header-scrollable-content-status-bar\">Classic Desktop Shell Recipe (Sidebar + Header + Scrollable Content + Status Bar)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> main() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    state = {<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;nav&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;search&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>}\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-com\"># Main horizontal body (GROW(1) fills everything above the status bar)</span>\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GROW</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>)):\n                <span class=\"tok-com\"># Fixed 220px sidebar</span>\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=<span class=\"tok-num\">220</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SURFACE_MUTED</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">4</span>):\n                    ctx.heading(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Workspace&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">4</span>)\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> i, (label, icon) <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> enumerate([\n                        (<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Overview&quot;</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">LAYOUT_DASHBOARD</span>),\n                        (<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Activity&quot;</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACTIVITY</span>),\n                        (<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Settings&quot;</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SETTINGS</span>),\n                    ]):\n                        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.nav_item(label, icon=icon, selected=(state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;nav&quot;</span>] == i), group=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;main&quot;</span>):\n                            state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;nav&quot;</span>] = i\n\n                <span class=\"tok-com\"># Flexible right content pane</span>\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n                    <span class=\"tok-com\"># Top header bar</span>\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad_x=<span class=\"tok-num\">20</span>, pad_y=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>):\n                        ctx.breadcrumb([<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Workspace&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Overview&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Activity&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Settings&quot;</span>][state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;nav&quot;</span>]]])\n                        ctx.spacer()  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Pushes everything after it to the right!</span>\n                        state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;search&quot;</span>] = ctx.search(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;q&quot;</span>, state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;search&quot;</span>], width=<span class=\"tok-num\">220</span>, size=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ControlSize</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SM</span>)\n                        ctx.theme_toggle()\n\n                    ctx.separator()\n\n                    <span class=\"tok-com\"># Responsive auto-wrapping card grid inside a scroll container</span>\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.scroll(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;body_scroll&quot;</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">20</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>):\n                        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.grid(columns=<span class=\"tok-num\">3</span>, min_column_width=<span class=\"tok-num\">180</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">14</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n                            <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> k <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> range(<span class=\"tok-num\">6</span>):\n                                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">6</span>):\n                                    ctx.secondary(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Node #{k + 1}&quot;</span>)\n                                    ctx.heading(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;{94 + k}.2%&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">3</span>)\n                                    ctx.badge(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Healthy&quot;</span>, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SUCCESS</span>, dot=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>)\n\n            <span class=\"tok-com\"># Bottom status bar</span>\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.status_bar():\n                ctx.status_bar_text(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Connected&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CIRCLE_CHECK</span>, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SUCCESS</span>)\n                ctx.status_bar_spacer()\n                ctx.status_bar_item(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;60 FPS&quot;</span>)\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">App</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Layout Recipe&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">960</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">620</span>, theme=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>, accent=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BLUE</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> app:\n        app.run(draw)\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    main()</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-3-procedural-decomposition-plain-functions-state-dict\">Lesson 3: Procedural Decomposition (Plain Functions + State Dict)</h2>\n<p>As a procedural app grows beyond ~100 lines, split your UI into plain functions that accept <code>(ctx: ui.UI, state: dict)</code>. Notice how readable, modular, and testable this is—no inheritance required:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw_toolbar(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>, state: dict) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.toolbar():\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.toolbar_button(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PLUS</span>, label=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;New Item&quot;</span>, tooltip=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Ctrl+N&quot;</span>):\n            state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;items&quot;</span>].append({<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Untitled&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;done&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>})\n        ctx.toolbar_separator()\n        state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;hide_done&quot;</span>] = ctx.toolbar_toggle(state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;hide_done&quot;</span>], ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILTER</span>, tooltip=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Hide completed&quot;</span>)\n        ctx.toolbar_spacer()\n        ctx.theme_toggle()\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw_item_list(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>, state: dict) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.scroll(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;items&quot;</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">20</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">8</span>):\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> idx, item <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> enumerate(state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;items&quot;</span>]):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;hide_done&quot;</span>] <span class=\"tok-kw\">and</span> item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;done&quot;</span>]:\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">continue</span>\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.id_scope(idx):\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>):\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>):\n                        item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;done&quot;</span>] = ctx.checkbox(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;##chk&quot;</span>, item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;done&quot;</span>])\n                        item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>] = ctx.inline_edit(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>, item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>], width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>)\n                        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.icon_button(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TRASH</span>, tooltip=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Remove&quot;</span>):\n                            state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;items&quot;</span>].pop(idx)\n                            <span class=\"tok-kw\">break</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-4-manual-frame-loop-while-app-frame\">Lesson 4: Manual Frame Loop (<code>while app.frame():</code>)</h2>\n<p><code>app.run(draw)</code> is simply a convenience loop around <code>app.frame()</code>. Whenever you want explicit per-frame control—for example, draining a network queue, stepping a physics simulation, or driving custom frame timing—write the <code>while app.frame():</code> loop directly:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">App</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Manual Loop&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">520</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">320</span>, theme=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>, accent=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">AMBER</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> app:\n    ctx = app.ui\n    clicks = <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">while</span> app.frame(wait=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>):\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.shortcut(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Mod</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Key</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Q</span>):\n            app.quit()\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n            ctx.heading(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Frame #{ctx.frame_count}&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)\n            ctx.secondary(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Delta time: {ctx.dt * 1000:.2f} ms  ·  Scale: {ctx.scale:.1f}x&quot;</span>)\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Trigger Toast&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BELL</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>):\n                clicks += <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>\n                ctx.toast(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Notification #{clicks}&quot;</span>, description=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Dispatched from manual loop&quot;</span>, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">INFO</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-5-complete-procedural-project-expense-budget-tracker\">Lesson 5: Complete Procedural Project — Expense &amp; Budget Tracker</h2>\n<p>Below is a complete, 100% standalone procedural application combining <strong>split panes</strong>, <strong>forms &amp; money input</strong>, **keyboard shortcuts (<code>Ctrl+K</code> command palette)<strong>, </strong>donut chart<strong>, and </strong>sortable table**:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Complete procedural project: Personal Expense &amp; Budget Tracker.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">from</span> __future__ <span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> annotations\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-cls\">CATEGORIES</span> = [<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Housing&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Food&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Transport&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Software&quot;</span>]\n<span class=\"tok-cls\">CAT_TONES</span> = [ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">VIOLET</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SUCCESS</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">INFO</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">WARNING</span>]\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw_form_pane(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>, st: dict) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SURFACE_MUTED</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">18</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">14</span>):\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>):\n            ctx.heading(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Add Expense&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">3</span>)\n            ctx.spacer()\n            ctx.theme_toggle()\n\n        st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>] = ctx.input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;exp_title&quot;</span>, st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>], label=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Description&quot;</span>, placeholder=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;e.g. Cloud hosting&quot;</span>)\n        st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;amount&quot;</span>] = ctx.money_input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;exp_amt&quot;</span>, st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;amount&quot;</span>], label=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Amount&quot;</span>, symbol=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;$&quot;</span>, code=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;USD&quot;</span>)\n        st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;cat&quot;</span>] = ctx.select(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;exp_cat&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-cls\">CATEGORIES</span>, st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;cat&quot;</span>], label=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Category&quot;</span>)\n\n        err = st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;error&quot;</span>]\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> err:\n            ctx.alert(err, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DANGER</span>)\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Record Expense&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PLUS</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>, full_width=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">not</span> st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>].strip():\n                st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;error&quot;</span>] = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Please enter a description.&quot;</span>\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">elif</span> st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;amount&quot;</span>] &lt;= <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>:\n                st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;error&quot;</span>] = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Amount must be greater than $0.00.&quot;</span>\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">else</span>:\n                st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;error&quot;</span>] = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>\n                st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;rows&quot;</span>].append((st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>].strip(), st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;cat&quot;</span>], round(st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;amount&quot;</span>], <span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)))\n                ctx.toast(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Expense added&quot;</span>, description=st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>].strip(), tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SUCCESS</span>)\n                st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>] = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>\n\n        ctx.separator()\n        totals = [sum(r[<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>] <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> r <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;rows&quot;</span>] <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> r[<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>] == c) <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> c <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> range(len(<span class=\"tok-cls\">CATEGORIES</span>))]\n        ctx.secondary(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Category Breakdown&quot;</span>)\n        ctx.donut_chart(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;cat_donut&quot;</span>, totals, <span class=\"tok-cls\">CATEGORIES</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">180</span>, format=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;$%.0f&quot;</span>)\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw_ledger_pane(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>, st: dict) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    total = sum(r[<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>] <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> r <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;rows&quot;</span>])\n    budget = <span class=\"tok-num\">2500.0</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>):\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GROW</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>), pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">6</span>):\n                ctx.secondary(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Total Spent&quot;</span>)\n                ctx.number_roll(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;spent_roll&quot;</span>, f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;${total:,.2f}&quot;</span>, font=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FontRole</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DISPLAY</span>, size=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>)\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GROW</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>), pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">8</span>):\n                ctx.meter(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Monthly Budget&quot;</span>, total, budget, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;USD&quot;</span>)\n\n        cols = [\n            ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TableColumn</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Description&quot;</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GROW</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>), sortable=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>),\n            ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TableColumn</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Category&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">130</span>),\n            ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TableColumn</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Amount&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">110</span>, align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TextAlign</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">RIGHT</span>, sortable=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>),\n        ]\n        rows = list(st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;rows&quot;</span>])\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;sort&quot;</span>].column == <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>:\n            rows.sort(key=<span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> r: r[<span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>].lower(), reverse=st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;sort&quot;</span>].descending)\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">elif</span> st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;sort&quot;</span>].column == <span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>:\n            rows.sort(key=<span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> r: r[<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>], reverse=st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;sort&quot;</span>].descending)\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.table(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;ledger_tbl&quot;</span>, cols, sort=st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;sort&quot;</span>], height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, striped=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> tbl:\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> tbl:\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> desc, cat_idx, amt <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> rows:\n                    tbl.row()\n                    tbl.cell_text(desc)\n                    tbl.cell()\n                    ctx.badge(<span class=\"tok-cls\">CATEGORIES</span>[cat_idx], tone=<span class=\"tok-cls\">CAT_TONES</span>[cat_idx], size=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ControlSize</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SM</span>)\n                    tbl.cell_text(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;${amt:,.2f}&quot;</span>)\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> tbl.sort is <span class=\"tok-kw\">not</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n            st[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;sort&quot;</span>] = tbl.sort\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> main() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    state = {\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;amount&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">49.00</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;cat&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">3</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;error&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;split&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">0.34</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;palette&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;sort&quot;</span>: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TableSort</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>, <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>),\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;rows&quot;</span>: [\n            (<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Apartment Rent&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">1250.00</span>),\n            (<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Weekly Groceries&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">142.80</span>),\n            (<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Metro Pass&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">65.00</span>),\n            (<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Dev Server &amp; Domains&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">3</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">38.50</span>),\n        ],\n    }\n    commands = [\n        ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Command</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Clear all expenses&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TRASH</span>, group=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Ledger&quot;</span>),\n        ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Command</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Toggle Dark/Light Theme&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">MOON</span>, group=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;View&quot;</span>, shortcut=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Ctrl D&quot;</span>),\n    ]\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.shortcut(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Mod</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Key</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">K</span>):\n            state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;palette&quot;</span>] = <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.split(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;root_split&quot;</span>, state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;split&quot;</span>], min_first=<span class=\"tok-num\">290</span>, min_second=<span class=\"tok-num\">420</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> sp:\n            draw_form_pane(ctx, state)\n            sp.next()\n            draw_ledger_pane(ctx, state)\n        state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;split&quot;</span>] = sp.ratio\n\n        state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;palette&quot;</span>], picked = ctx.command_palette(state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;palette&quot;</span>], commands)\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> picked == <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>:\n            state[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;rows&quot;</span>].clear()\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">elif</span> picked == <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>:\n            ctx.theme_mode = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">LIGHT</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.theme_mode == ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">else</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">App</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Budget Ledger — nexa&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">1020</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">660</span>, theme=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>, accent=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GREEN</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> app:\n        app.run(draw)\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    main()</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next Steps</h2>\n<p>Ready to scale up to multi-screen applications with reusable custom components, routing history, and reactive stores? Continue to <strong><a href=\"#tutorial-oop\" data-doc-link=\"tutorial-oop\">Object-Oriented (OOP) Architecture →</a></strong>.</p>", "toc": [{"title": "Lesson 1: Top-Level Functional Basics", "id": "lesson-1-top-level-functional-basics"}, {"title": "Lesson 2: Mastering Flexbox, Sizing & Grids", "id": "lesson-2-mastering-flexbox-sizing-grids"}, {"title": "Lesson 3: Procedural Decomposition (Plain Functions + State Dict)", "id": "lesson-3-procedural-decomposition-plain-functions-state-dict"}, {"title": "Lesson 4: Manual Frame Loop (while app.frame():)", "id": "lesson-4-manual-frame-loop-while-app-frame"}, {"title": "Lesson 5: Complete Procedural Project — Expense & Budget Tracker", "id": "lesson-5-complete-procedural-project-expense-budget-tracker"}, {"title": "Next Steps", "id": "next-steps"}]}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "title": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "group": "Tutorials", "source": "docs/tutorial-oop.md", "html": "<h1 id=\"tutorial-object-oriented-oop-architecture\">Tutorial: Object-Oriented (OOP) Architecture</h1>\n<p>When your application grows into multiple views, reusable widget cards, shared state stores, and background workers, <code>nexa</code> provides a clean, zero-boilerplate Object-Oriented layer built directly on top of its immediate-mode engine:</p>\n<ul><li>**<code>ui.Application</code>** — Top-level application class managing the native <code>App</code> window, <code>Router</code>, <code>BackgroundRunner</code>, and lifecycle (<code>setup</code>, <code>build</code>, <code>on_close</code>).</li><li>**<code>ui.Component</code><strong> — Reusable, stateful or stateless UI building block with </strong>automatic ID-scope isolation** (<code>on_mount</code>, <code>build</code>, <code>on_unmount</code>).</li><li>**<code>ui.View</code><strong> &amp; </strong><code>ui.Router</code>** — Named screens with parameterized navigation (<code>push</code>, <code>replace</code>, <code>back</code>, <code>forward</code>) and <code>on_enter</code> / <code>on_leave</code> hooks.</li><li>**<code>ui.Store[T]</code>** — Observable state container with <code>update()</code>, <code>subscribe()</code>, and automatic native event-loop wakeup.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"functional-procedural-vs-oop-side-by-side\">Functional/Procedural vs. OOP: Side-by-Side</h2>\n<p>Both paradigms call the <strong>exact same widget methods</strong> and can even be mixed inside the same frame!</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Functional / Procedural (<code>ui.run</code> / plain <code>def</code>)</th><th>Object-Oriented (<code>Application</code> / <code>Component</code> / <code>View</code>)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Best for</strong></td><td>Scripts, single-window utilities, data dashboards, quick tools</td><td>Multi-screen desktop apps, reusable widget libraries, team codebases</td></tr><tr><td><strong>State storage</strong></td><td>Closures (<code>nonlocal</code>) or passed <code>dict</code> / state objects</td><td>Instance attributes (<code>self.count</code>) and shared <code>ui.Store[T]</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Widget ID scoping</strong></td><td>Manual <code>with ctx.id_scope(key):</code> in loops</td><td><strong>Automatic</strong>—every <code>Component(key)</code> scopes all child widgets!</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Screen routing</strong></td><td><code>if tab == 0: ... elif tab == 1: ...</code></td><td><code>self.router.push(&quot;project&quot;, id=42)</code> + <code>back()</code> / <code>forward()</code> history</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Background workers</strong></td><td><code>runner = ui.BackgroundRunner.for_app(app)</code></td><td>Built-in <code>self.runner</code> &amp; lazy <code>self.async_bridge</code> on <code>Application</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-1-subclassing-ui-application\">Lesson 1: Subclassing <code>ui.Application</code></h2>\n<p>You can configure window defaults either as <strong>class attributes</strong> or via **<code>super().__init__(...)</code>** arguments:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">CounterApp</span>(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Application</span>):\n    title = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;OOP Counter&quot;</span>\n    width = <span class=\"tok-num\">560</span>\n    height = <span class=\"tok-num\">360</span>\n    theme = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>\n    accent = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">VIOLET</span>  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Real accents: NEUTRAL, VIOLET, BLUE, GREEN, AMBER, ORANGE, CORAL, ROSE</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> setup(self) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-com\"># Called automatically at the end of __init__</span>\n        self.count = <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>\n        self.step = <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> build(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">28</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n            ctx.heading(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Total: {self.count}&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>)\n            self.step = int(ctx.slider(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Step size&quot;</span>, self.step, <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>, step=<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>, show_value=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>, format=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;%.0f&quot;</span>))\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>):\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Add +{self.step}&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PLUS</span>):\n                    self.count += self.step\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Reset&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GHOST</span>):\n                    self.count = <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> on_close(self) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-com\"># Optional cleanup when the window closes</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">pass</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    <span class=\"tok-cls\">CounterApp</span>().run()</code></pre></div>\n<p>You can also override <code>__init__</code> and pass <code>title</code>, <code>width</code>, <code>height</code>, <code>theme</code>, <code>accent</code> directly to <code>super().__init__(&quot;Custom Title&quot;, width=720, height=420, accent=ui.Accent.GREEN)</code>.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-2-reusable-ui-component-automatic-id-isolation\">Lesson 2: Reusable <code>ui.Component</code> &amp; Automatic ID Isolation</h2>\n<p>In raw immediate-mode UIs, rendering two components that both contain <code>ctx.button(&quot;Increment&quot;)</code> would normally collide on the ID <code>&quot;Increment&quot;</code>.</p>\n<p><code>ui.Component</code> solves this automatically: calling <code>my_component(ctx)</code> (or <code>my_component()</code> inside a frame) wraps <code>build(ctx)</code> inside <code>with ctx.id_scope(self.key):</code>—and runs <code>on_mount(ctx)</code> once on first render!</p>\n<p>Even better: **<code>build(self, ctx)</code> can return a value**, so parent views can react to component events naturally!</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">PipelineCard</span>(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Component</span>):\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> __init__(self, key: str, title: str, initial_rpm: int = <span class=\"tok-num\">120</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        super().__init__(key)  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Pushes `key` onto CUI&#x27;s ID stack every render!</span>\n        self.title = title\n        self.rpm = initial_rpm\n        self.enabled = <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> on_mount(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-com\"># Runs once before the very first build()</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">pass</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> build(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; bool:\n        <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Render the card and return True if the &#x27;Restart&#x27; button was clicked.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n        restarted = <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">18</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GROW</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>)):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>):\n                ctx.heading(self.title, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">4</span>)\n                ctx.spacer()\n                <span class=\"tok-com\"># Notice both cards have a switch &amp; buttons with the SAME labels—zero collision!</span>\n                self.enabled = ctx.switch(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;##on&quot;</span>, self.enabled)\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.disabled_scope(<span class=\"tok-kw\">not</span> self.enabled):\n                self.rpm = int(ctx.slider(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Target RPM&quot;</span>, self.rpm, <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">500</span>, step=<span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>, show_value=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>, format=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;%.0f&quot;</span>))\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">8</span>):\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Boost +50&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ZAP</span>, size=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ControlSize</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SM</span>):\n                        self.rpm = min(<span class=\"tok-num\">500</span>, self.rpm + <span class=\"tok-num\">50</span>)\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Restart&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">OUTLINE</span>, size=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ControlSize</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SM</span>):\n                        restarted = <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">return</span> restarted\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">DualPipelineApp</span>(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Application</span>):\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> __init__(self) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        super().__init__(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Dual Pipelines&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">760</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">380</span>, theme=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>, accent=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GREEN</span>)\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> setup(self) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        self.left = <span class=\"tok-cls\">PipelineCard</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;pipe_a&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Ingestion Cluster&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">180</span>)\n        self.right = <span class=\"tok-cls\">PipelineCard</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;pipe_b&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Inference Workers&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">320</span>)\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> build(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">18</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> self.left(ctx):\n                ctx.toast(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Restarted Ingestion Cluster&quot;</span>, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">INFO</span>)\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> self.right(ctx):\n                ctx.toast(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Restarted Inference Workers&quot;</span>, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">INFO</span>)\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    <span class=\"tok-cls\">DualPipelineApp</span>().run()</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-3-multi-screen-navigation-with-ui-view-ui-router\">Lesson 3: Multi-Screen Navigation with <code>ui.View</code> &amp; <code>ui.Router</code></h2>\n<p>Every <code>ui.Application</code> comes with <code>self.router</code> pre-wired to wake the window on navigation:</p>\n<ul><li>**<code>self.router.register(&quot;route_name&quot;, MyView(...))</code>** — Register a <code>View</code> instance (the first registered route becomes active automatically).</li><li>**<code>self.router.push(&quot;detail&quot;, item_id=42)</code>** — Navigate forward, passing arbitrary keyword parameters to <code>DetailView.on_enter(params)</code>.</li><li>**<code>self.router.replace(&quot;login&quot;)</code>** — Replace the current history entry without growing the back stack.</li><li>**<code>self.router.back()</code> / <code>self.router.forward()</code>** — Navigate browser-style history (<code>can_go_back</code>, <code>can_go_forward</code>).</li><li>**<code>self.router.render(ctx)</code>** — Render whichever <code>View</code> is currently active.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">ProjectDetailView</span>(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">View</span>):\n    title = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Project Detail&quot;</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> __init__(self, router: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Router</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        super().__init__(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;detail&quot;</span>)\n        self.router = router\n        self.project_id: int = -<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> on_enter(self, params: dict) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        self.project_id = params.get(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;project_id&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>)\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> on_leave(self) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">pass</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> build(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Back&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ARROW_LEFT</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GHOST</span>):\n                self.router.back()\n            ctx.heading(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Inspecting Project #{self.project_id}&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-4-reactive-state-with-ui-store-t\">Lesson 4: Reactive State with <code>ui.Store[T]</code></h2>\n<p>In multi-view OOP apps, passing raw dicts between 6 views can get messy. <code>ui.Store[T]</code> holds shared state, notifies subscribers on change, and automatically wakes the UI window when mutated:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>store = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Store</span>({<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Filter&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;incidents&quot;</span>: []}, wake=self.wake)\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># Read current state</span>\nitems = store.value[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;incidents&quot;</span>]\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># Mutate in-place OR return a new value — both notify subscribers and wake the window!</span>\nstore.update(<span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> s: s[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;incidents&quot;</span>].append({<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;API spike&quot;</span>}))</code></pre></div>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Thread-safety tip:</strong> When updating a <code>Store</code> from a background worker thread, marshal the mutation via <code>self.call_soon(lambda: store.update(...))</code> (or <code>on_done=</code> in <code>self.runner.submit(...)</code>) so state only mutates between UI frames!</p></blockquote>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"lesson-5-complete-oop-capstone-incident-response-console\">Lesson 5: Complete OOP Capstone — Incident Response Console</h2>\n<p>Here is a complete, 100% standalone multi-view OOP application combining **<code>Application</code><strong>, </strong><code>Store</code><strong>, </strong><code>Router</code><strong>, </strong>two <code>View</code> screens (<code>OverviewView</code> &amp; <code>DetailView</code>)<strong>, </strong>reusable <code>IncidentCard</code> <code>Component</code>s<strong>, </strong>live accent switching<strong>, and </strong>background diagnostics via <code>self.runner</code>**:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Complete OOP Capstone: Multi-View Incident Response Console.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">from</span> __future__ <span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> annotations\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> time\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">IncidentCard</span>(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Component</span>):\n    <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Reusable incident summary card with automatic ID scoping.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> __init__(self, incident_id: int) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        super().__init__(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;inc_{incident_id}&quot;</span>)\n        self.incident_id = incident_id\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> build(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>, item: dict) -&gt; str | <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        action: str | <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span> = <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>\n        tone = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SUCCESS</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolved&quot;</span>] <span class=\"tok-kw\">else</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DANGER</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>):\n                ctx.badge(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Resolved&quot;</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolved&quot;</span>] <span class=\"tok-kw\">else</span> <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Open&quot;</span>, tone=tone, dot=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>)\n                ctx.text(item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>], font=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FontRole</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">MEDIUM</span>, size=<span class=\"tok-num\">15</span>)\n                ctx.spacer()\n                ctx.muted(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#{item[&#x27;id&#x27;]} · {item[&#x27;service&#x27;]}&quot;</span>)\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">8</span>):\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Inspect&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ARROW_RIGHT</span>, size=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ControlSize</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SM</span>):\n                    action = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;inspect&quot;</span>\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">not</span> item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolved&quot;</span>]:\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Resolve&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CHECK</span>, size=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ControlSize</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SM</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>):\n                        action = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolve&quot;</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">return</span> action\n\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">OverviewView</span>(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">View</span>):\n    title = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Incidents&quot;</span>\n    icon = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACTIVITY</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> __init__(self, store: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Store</span>[dict], router: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Router</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        super().__init__(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;overview&quot;</span>)\n        self.store = store\n        self.router = router\n        self.cards: dict[int, <span class=\"tok-cls\">IncidentCard</span>] = {}\n        self.new_title = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>\n        self.new_service = <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> _create_incident(self, title: str, service: str) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> _mutate(s: dict) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n            s[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;incidents&quot;</span>].insert(<span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>, {\n                <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;id&quot;</span>: s[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;next_id&quot;</span>],\n                <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>: title,\n                <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;service&quot;</span>: service,\n                <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolved&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>,\n                <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;notes&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Investigating root cause.&quot;</span>,\n            })\n            s[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;next_id&quot;</span>] += <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>\n\n        self.store.update(_mutate)\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> build(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        services = [<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Auth API&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Edge Gateway&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Billing DB&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Search Index&quot;</span>]\n        items = self.store.value[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;incidents&quot;</span>]\n        open_cnt = sum(<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> x <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> items <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">not</span> x[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolved&quot;</span>])\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">18</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.grid(columns=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>, min_column_width=<span class=\"tok-num\">220</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">14</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">4</span>):\n                    ctx.secondary(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Active Incidents&quot;</span>)\n                    ctx.heading(str(open_cnt), level=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">4</span>):\n                    ctx.secondary(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Total Logged&quot;</span>)\n                    ctx.heading(str(len(items)), level=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n                ctx.label(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Report New Incident&quot;</span>)\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>, align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">END</span>, wrap=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>):\n                    self.new_title = ctx.input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>, self.new_title, placeholder=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Describe issue...&quot;</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GROW</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>))\n                    self.new_service = ctx.select(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;svc&quot;</span>, services, self.new_service, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">160</span>)\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Create&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PLUS</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>):\n                        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> self.new_title.strip():\n                            self._create_incident(self.new_title.strip(), services[self.new_service])\n                            self.new_title = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> item <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> items:\n                iid = item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;id&quot;</span>]\n                card = self.cards.setdefault(iid, <span class=\"tok-cls\">IncidentCard</span>(iid))\n                <span class=\"tok-com\"># Invoke Component.build inside its automatic ID scope!</span>\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.id_scope(card.key):\n                    act = card.build(ctx, item)\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> act == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;inspect&quot;</span>:\n                    self.router.push(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;detail&quot;</span>, id=iid)\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">elif</span> act == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolve&quot;</span>:\n                    self.store.update(<span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> s, target=iid: next(\n                        x.__setitem__(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolved&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> x <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> s[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;incidents&quot;</span>] <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> x[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;id&quot;</span>] == target\n                    ))\n                    ctx.toast(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Incident #{iid} marked resolved&quot;</span>, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SUCCESS</span>)\n\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">DetailView</span>(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">View</span>):\n    title = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Detail&quot;</span>\n    icon = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILE_TEXT</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> __init__(self, store: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Store</span>[dict], router: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Router</span>, runner: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BackgroundRunner</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        super().__init__(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;detail&quot;</span>)\n        self.store = store\n        self.router = router\n        self.runner = runner\n        self.current_id = -<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>\n        self.diag_task: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TaskHandle</span> | <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span> = <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> on_enter(self, params: dict) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        self.current_id = params.get(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;id&quot;</span>, -<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>)\n        self.diag_task = <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> build(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        item = next((x <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> x <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> self.store.value[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;incidents&quot;</span>] <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> x[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;id&quot;</span>] == self.current_id), <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>)\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> item is <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n            ctx.empty_state(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Incident not found&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">INBOX</span>)\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">return</span>\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>):\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Back to list&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ARROW_LEFT</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">GHOST</span>):\n                    self.router.back()\n                ctx.spacer()\n                status = self.diag_task.button_status <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> self.diag_task <span class=\"tok-kw\">else</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Status</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">IDLE</span>\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.status_button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Run Diagnostics&quot;</span>, status, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TERMINAL</span>):\n                    self.diag_task = self.runner.submit(\n                        <span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span>: (time.sleep(<span class=\"tok-num\">0.35</span>), <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Latency p99=14ms, 0 packet drops&quot;</span>)[<span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>],\n                        on_done=<span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> report: self.store.update(\n                            <span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> _s: item.__setitem__(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;notes&quot;</span>, item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;notes&quot;</span>] + f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;\\n[Diag] {report}&quot;</span>)\n                        ),\n                    )\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">20</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n                ctx.heading(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#{item[&#x27;id&#x27;]} — {item[&#x27;title&#x27;]}&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)\n                ctx.secondary(f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Service: {item[&#x27;service&#x27;]}&quot;</span>)\n                item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;notes&quot;</span>] = ctx.textarea(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;notes&quot;</span>, item[<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;notes&quot;</span>], label=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Runbook Notes&quot;</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">160</span>)\n\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">IncidentConsoleApp</span>(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Application</span>):\n    title = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Incident Console — nexa OOP&quot;</span>\n    width = <span class=\"tok-num\">960</span>\n    height = <span class=\"tok-num\">660</span>\n    theme = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>\n    accent = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CORAL</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> setup(self) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        self.store = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Store</span>(\n            {\n                <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;next_id&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">103</span>,\n                <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;incidents&quot;</span>: [\n                    {<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">102</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Elevated TLS handshake latency in EU-West&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;service&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Edge Gateway&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolved&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;notes&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Checking upstream edge pop.&quot;</span>},\n                    {<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;id&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">101</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;title&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Read replica lag cleared after compaction&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;service&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Billing DB&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;resolved&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;notes&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Auto-compaction finished in 18s.&quot;</span>},\n                ],\n            },\n            wake=self.wake,\n        )\n        self.router.register(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;overview&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-cls\">OverviewView</span>(self.store, self.router))\n        self.router.register(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;detail&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-cls\">DetailView</span>(self.store, self.router, self.runner))\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> build(self, ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad_x=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, pad_y=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>):\n                ctx.icon(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SHIELD</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">18</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACCENT</span>)\n                ctx.text(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Incident Console&quot;</span>, font=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FontRole</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">MEDIUM</span>, size=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>)\n                ctx.spacer()\n                accents = [ui.accent_name(a).capitalize() <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> a <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>]\n                picked = ctx.select(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;acc_sel&quot;</span>, accents, int(ctx.accent), width=<span class=\"tok-num\">130</span>)\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> picked != int(ctx.accent):\n                    ctx.accent = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>(picked)\n                ctx.theme_toggle()\n\n            ctx.separator()\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.scroll(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;main_scroll&quot;</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>):\n                self.router.render(ctx)\n\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    <span class=\"tok-cls\">IncidentConsoleApp</span>().run()</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next Steps</h2>\n<ul><li>Learn every detail of <strong>Accents, Tones, OKLCH Color Tokens, Custom Fonts, and Icons</strong> in <strong><a href=\"#theming-and-styling\" data-doc-link=\"theming-and-styling\">Theming &amp; Styling →</a></strong>.</li><li>Add <strong>async HTTP APIs, streaming LLMs, and multi-threaded workers</strong> in <strong><a href=\"#concurrency-and-async\" data-doc-link=\"concurrency-and-async\">Concurrency &amp; Async →</a></strong>.</li></ul>", "toc": [{"title": "Functional/Procedural vs. OOP: Side-by-Side", "id": "functional-procedural-vs-oop-side-by-side"}, {"title": "Lesson 1: Subclassing ui.Application", "id": "lesson-1-subclassing-ui-application"}, {"title": "Lesson 2: Reusable ui.Component & Automatic ID Isolation", "id": "lesson-2-reusable-ui-component-automatic-id-isolation"}, {"title": "Lesson 3: Multi-Screen Navigation with ui.View & ui.Router", "id": "lesson-3-multi-screen-navigation-with-ui-view-ui-router"}, {"title": "Lesson 4: Reactive State with ui.Store[T]", "id": "lesson-4-reactive-state-with-ui-store-t"}, {"title": "Lesson 5: Complete OOP Capstone — Incident Response Console", "id": "lesson-5-complete-oop-capstone-incident-response-console"}, {"title": "Next Steps", "id": "next-steps"}]}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "title": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "group": "Core Guides", "source": "docs/theming-and-styling.md", "html": "<h1 id=\"theming-accents-tones-colors-typography\">Theming, Accents, Tones, Colors &amp; Typography</h1>\n<p><code>nexa</code> ships with a perceptually calibrated <strong>OKLCH / OKLab</strong> design system out of the box—complete with smooth Light/Dark cross-fading, **8 built-in <code>Accent</code> palettes<strong>, </strong>9 semantic <code>Tone</code>s<strong>, </strong>34 live-editable <code>Token</code> slots<strong>, embedded </strong>Inter<strong> &amp; </strong>Geist Mono<strong> typography, and </strong>168 Lucide vector icons**.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"1-light-dark-theme-modes-ui-thememode\">1. Light &amp; Dark Theme Modes (<code>ui.ThemeMode</code>)</h2>\n<p>Switch between Light and Dark modes at startup or dynamically at runtime (surfaces and text smoothly interpolate across frames):</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># At window creation:</span>\napp = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">App</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Demo&quot;</span>, theme=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>, accent=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">VIOLET</span>)\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># Inside any frame:</span>\nctx.theme_mode = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">LIGHT</span>  <span class=\"tok-com\"># or ui.ThemeMode.DARK</span>\nctx.theme_toggle()                   <span class=\"tok-com\"># Built-in animated Sun/Moon icon button!</span>\nmode = ctx.theme_switcher(mode)      <span class=\"tok-com\"># 2-segment Light/Dark pill switcher</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"2-the-8-built-in-ui-accent-palettes\">2. The 8 Built-In <code>ui.Accent</code> Palettes</h2>\n<p><code>ui.Accent</code> defines <strong>exactly 8 built-in primary highlight palettes</strong> (matching CUI&#x27;s <code>cui_accent</code> enum <code>0..7</code>):</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Enum Member</th><th>Value</th><th><code>ui.accent_name(...)</code></th><th>Dark Mode Hex</th><th>Light Mode Hex</th><th>Character</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ui.Accent.NEUTRAL</code></td><td><code>0</code></td><td><code>&quot;neutral&quot;</code></td><td><code>#e8e8e8</code></td><td><code>#1d1d1d</code></td><td>Monochrome ink / high-contrast editorial</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Accent.VIOLET</code></td><td><code>1</code></td><td><code>&quot;violet&quot;</code></td><td><code>#a78bff</code></td><td><code>#7747ff</code></td><td>Creative tools, AI workspaces</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Accent.BLUE</code></td><td><code>2</code></td><td><code>&quot;blue&quot;</code></td><td><code>#6ba3ff</code></td><td><code>#0562ef</code></td><td>Default desktop primary accent</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Accent.GREEN</code></td><td><code>3</code></td><td><code>&quot;green&quot;</code></td><td><code>#53dca6</code></td><td><code>#00864b</code></td><td>Finance, emerald/mint telemetry</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Accent.AMBER</code></td><td><code>4</code></td><td><code>&quot;amber&quot;</code></td><td><code>#ffcb62</code></td><td><code>#f3ad20</code></td><td>Warm gold instrumentation</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Accent.ORANGE</code></td><td><code>5</code></td><td><code>&quot;orange&quot;</code></td><td><code>#ffad5e</code></td><td><code>#c25300</code></td><td>Industrial / hardware studio</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Accent.CORAL</code></td><td><code>6</code></td><td><code>&quot;coral&quot;</code></td><td><code>#ff9386</code></td><td><code>#d1403a</code></td><td>Media players, warm creative apps</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Accent.ROSE</code></td><td><code>7</code></td><td><code>&quot;rose&quot;</code></td><td><code>#ff8bc5</code></td><td><code>#d23286</code></td><td>Vibrant magenta / pink highlight</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Important:</strong> Only those 8 members exist on <code>ui.Accent</code> (<code>NEUTRAL</code>, <code>VIOLET</code>, <code>BLUE</code>, <code>GREEN</code>, <code>AMBER</code>, <code>ORANGE</code>, <code>CORAL</code>, <code>ROSE</code>). Names like <code>Accent.MINT</code>, <code>Accent.CYAN</code>, or <code>Accent.TEAL</code> do <strong>not</strong> exist on <code>ui.Accent</code> (<code>GREEN</code> is an emerald-mint <code>#53dca6</code> in dark mode, and <code>Tone.TEAL</code> exists on <code>ui.Tone</code> for badges/events!). Want <strong>any custom hex or OKLCH brand color</strong> (such as Mint <code>#10b981</code> or Cyan <code>#06b6d4</code>) as your app&#x27;s primary accent? Override <code>Token.ACCENT</code> directly on <code>ctx.theme</code>—see Section 4 below!</p></blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"enumerating-all-accents-dynamically\">Enumerating All Accents Dynamically</h3>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-com\"># Clean Python iteration over all 8 accents:</span>\nlabels = [ui.accent_name(a).capitalize() <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> a <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>]\nchosen = ctx.segmented(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;accent_picker&quot;</span>, labels, int(ctx.accent))\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> chosen != int(ctx.accent):\n    ctx.accent = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>(chosen)</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"3-semantic-ui-tones-badges-alerts-toasts-kanban-gantt\">3. Semantic <code>ui.Tone</code>s (Badges, Alerts, Toasts, Kanban, Gantt)</h2>\n<p>While <code>ui.Accent</code> controls the <em>entire window&#x27;s</em> primary highlight palette, **<code>ui.Tone</code>** colors individual status elements (<code>badge</code>, <code>alert</code>, <code>banner</code>, <code>toast</code>, <code>CalEvent</code>, <code>GanttTask</code>, <code>SwipeAction</code>, <code>status_bar_text</code>) so semantic meanings stay consistent regardless of theme:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th><code>ui.Tone</code> Member</th><th>Typical Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.NEUTRAL</code></td><td>Default subtle chip/tag</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.INFO</code></td><td>Informational sky-blue notice</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.SUCCESS</code></td><td>Completed, paid, online, passing</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.WARNING</code></td><td>Pending, degraded, caution</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.DANGER</code></td><td>Error, destructive action, overdue</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.VIOLET</code></td><td>Category tag / purple highlight</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.TEAL</code></td><td>Category tag / teal-mint highlight</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.ROSE</code></td><td>Category tag / rose highlight</td></tr><tr><td><code>ui.Tone.ACCENT</code></td><td>Tracks whichever <code>ui.Accent</code> is currently active</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"4-custom-brand-colors-live-token-overrides-perceptual-oklch\">4. Custom Brand Colors, Live <code>Token</code> Overrides &amp; Perceptual OKLCH</h2>\n<p>Every color in <code>nexa</code> can be passed as:</p>\n<ul><li>A **<code>ui.Color(r, g, b, a=255)</code>** value</li><li>A hex string: **<code>&quot;#10b981&quot;</code><strong> or </strong><code>ui.Color.hex(&quot;#10b981&quot;)</code>** (6-digit <code>#RRGGBB</code> or 8-digit <code>#RRGGBBAA</code>)</li><li>An RGB/RGBA tuple: **<code>(16, 185, 129)</code><strong> or </strong><code>(16, 185, 129, 200)</code>**</li><li>A live semantic **<code>ui.Token</code><strong> or </strong><code>ui.Color.ACCENT</code><strong> / </strong><code>ui.Color.BACKGROUND</code><strong> / </strong><code>ui.Color.SURFACE</code><strong> / </strong><code>ui.Color.series(0..5)</code>** (resolved dynamically against the current Light/Dark theme!)</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"customizing-any-theme-token-live-ctx-theme\">Customizing Any Theme Token Live (<code>ctx.theme[...]</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-com\"># Set a custom Mint/Cyan brand palette on top of Dark mode:</span>\nctx.theme[ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Token</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACCENT</span>] = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.hex(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#14b8a6&quot;</span>)\nctx.theme[ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Token</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACCENT_STRONG</span>] = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.hex(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#2dd4bf&quot;</span>)\nctx.theme[ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Token</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACCENT_SUBTLE</span>] = ui.with_alpha(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#14b8a6&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">0.16</span>)\nctx.theme[ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Token</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACCENT_FOREGROUND</span>] = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.hex(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#042f2e&quot;</span>)\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># Tweak corner roundness &amp; UI scale:</span>\nctx.theme.radius_control = <span class=\"tok-num\">8.0</span>   <span class=\"tok-com\"># Buttons, inputs, selects</span>\nctx.theme.radius_surface = <span class=\"tok-num\">14.0</span>  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Cards</span>\nctx.theme.radius_panel = <span class=\"tok-num\">16.0</span>    <span class=\"tok-com\"># Dialogs, popovers, sheets</span>\nctx.font_scale = <span class=\"tok-num\">1.10</span>            <span class=\"tok-com\"># 110% proportional DPI/typography scale</span>\nctx.set_reduced_motion(<span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>)    <span class=\"tok-com\"># True snaps animations for accessibility</span></code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"perceptual-color-math-oklch-mix-colors-with-alpha\">Perceptual Color Math (<code>oklch</code>, <code>mix_colors</code>, <code>with_alpha</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>brand = ui.oklch(<span class=\"tok-num\">0.68</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">0.16</span>, <span class=\"tok-num\">172.0</span>)              <span class=\"tok-com\"># Perceptually uniform Lightness, Chroma, Hue°</span>\nsoft = ui.mix_colors(brand, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.hex(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#ffffff&quot;</span>), <span class=\"tok-num\">0.25</span>)  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Mixed in OKLab space (no muddy grays!)</span>\ntranslucent = ui.with_alpha(brand, <span class=\"tok-num\">0.20</span>)         <span class=\"tok-com\"># Multiply alpha by 0.20</span></code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"all-34-ui-token-slots\">All 34 <code>ui.Token</code> Slots</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Surfaces</strong>: <code>BACKGROUND</code>, <code>SURFACE</code>, <code>SURFACE_RAISED</code>, <code>SURFACE_MUTED</code></li><li><strong>Text</strong>: <code>FOREGROUND</code>, <code>TEXT_SECONDARY</code>, <code>TEXT_MUTED</code></li><li><strong>Borders</strong>: <code>BORDER</code>, <code>BORDER_SUBTLE</code>, <code>BORDER_STRONG</code></li><li><strong>Accent</strong>: <code>ACCENT</code>, <code>ACCENT_STRONG</code>, <code>ACCENT_SUBTLE</code>, <code>ACCENT_FOREGROUND</code></li><li><strong>Semantic</strong>: <code>SUCCESS</code>, <code>WARNING</code>, <code>DANGER</code>, <code>INFO</code></li><li><strong>Controls</strong>: <code>CONTROL_ON</code>, <code>CONTROL_GLYPH</code>, <code>CONTROL_TRACK</code>, <code>CONTROL_TRACK_HOVER</code>, <code>CONTROL_THUMB</code>, <code>CONTROL_THUMB_ON</code></li><li><strong>States</strong>: <code>HOVER</code>, <code>ACTIVE</code>, <code>SCRIM</code>, <code>FOCUS_RING</code></li><li><strong>Data Viz</strong>: <code>SERIES_1</code>, <code>SERIES_2</code>, <code>SERIES_3</code>, <code>SERIES_4</code>, <code>SERIES_5</code>, <code>SERIES_6</code></li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"5-typography-custom-ttf-fonts-international-fallback\">5. Typography, Custom <code>.ttf</code> Fonts &amp; International Fallback</h2>\n<p>Out of the box, <code>nexa</code> embeds:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Inter</strong> (<code>FontRole.BODY</code>, <code>FontRole.MEDIUM</code>, <code>FontRole.DISPLAY</code>)</li><li><strong>Geist Mono</strong> (<code>FontRole.MONO</code>)</li><li><strong>Lucide</strong> (<code>FontRole.ICONS</code> — <code>168</code> crisp vector icons)</li></ul>\n<p>To load your own <code>.ttf</code> / <code>.otf</code> typeface or add CJK / Arabic / Persian / Emoji fallback chains:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-com\"># Load primary UI font from file or bytes:</span>\nregular_id = ctx.font_load_file(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;assets/PlusJakartaSans-Regular.ttf&quot;</span>)\nctx.font_set_role(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FontRole</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BODY</span>, regular_id)\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># Attach an international fallback font so missing glyphs fall through seamlessly:</span>\nrtl_or_cjk_id = ctx.font_load_file(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;assets/Vazirmatn-Regular.ttf&quot;</span>)\nctx.font_add_fallback(regular_id, rtl_or_cjk_id)</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"6-icons-ui-icon\">6. Icons (<code>ui.Icon</code>)</h2>\n<p>All <strong>168 bundled Lucide icons</strong> are UTF-8 string constants on <code>ui.Icon</code> and can be passed to <code>icon=</code>, <code>ui.icon(...)</code>, <code>ui.icon_button(...)</code>, <code>ui.nav_item(...)</code>, or looked up dynamically by name:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ui.icon(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SPARKLES</span>, size=<span class=\"tok-num\">20</span>, color=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ACCENT</span>)\nui.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Deploy&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ROCKET</span>, icon_right=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ARROW_UP_RIGHT</span>)\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># Dynamic lookup (case-insensitive, supports kebab/snake case):</span>\nglyph = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.get(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;arrow-right&quot;</span>)  <span class=\"tok-com\"># -&gt; ui.Icon.ARROW_RIGHT</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Popular icons include:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Navigation &amp; Arrows</strong>: <code>ARROW_LEFT</code>, <code>ARROW_RIGHT</code>, <code>ARROW_UP</code>, <code>ARROW_DOWN</code>, <code>ARROW_UP_RIGHT</code>, <code>CHEVRON_LEFT</code>, <code>CHEVRON_RIGHT</code>, <code>CHEVRON_DOWN</code>, <code>CHEVRON_UP</code>, <code>HOUSE</code>, <code>MENU</code>, <code>PANEL_LEFT</code>, <code>EXTERNAL_LINK</code></li><li><strong>Actions &amp; Editing</strong>: <code>PLUS</code>, <code>MINUS</code>, <code>X</code>, <code>CHECK</code>, <code>SEARCH</code>, <code>EDIT</code> / <code>SQUARE_PEN</code>, <code>COPY</code>, <code>TRASH</code> / <code>TRASH_2</code>, <code>SAVE</code> / <code>DOWNLOAD</code>, <code>UPLOAD</code>, <code>SHARE_2</code>, <code>REFRESH_CW</code>, <code>FILTER</code>, <code>SLIDERS_HORIZONTAL</code>, <code>SETTINGS</code></li><li><strong>Files, Code &amp; Dev</strong>: <code>FILE</code>, <code>FILE_TEXT</code>, <code>FOLDER</code>, <code>CODE</code>, <code>TERMINAL</code>, <code>GIT_BRANCH</code>, <code>DATABASE</code>, <code>CPU</code>, <code>LAYERS</code>, <code>GRID_3X3</code>, <code>COMMAND</code>, <code>BUG</code></li><li><strong>Status, Security &amp; Social</strong>: <code>CIRCLE_CHECK</code>, <code>CIRCLE_ALERT</code>, <code>TRIANGLE_ALERT</code>, <code>INFO</code>, <code>SHIELD</code>, <code>LOCK</code>, <code>USER</code>, <code>USERS</code>, <code>MAIL</code>, <code>BELL</code>, <code>HEART</code>, <code>STAR</code>, <code>PIN</code> / <code>BOOKMARK</code>, <code>THUMBS_UP</code>, <code>THUMBS_DOWN</code>, <code>SEND</code></li><li><strong>Media, AI &amp; Theme</strong>: <code>SPARKLES</code>, <code>ZAP</code>, <code>PLAY</code>, <code>PAUSE</code>, <code>VOLUME_2</code>, <code>MIC</code>, <code>IMAGE</code>, <code>CALENDAR</code>, <code>CLOCK</code>, <code>GLOBE</code>, <code>WIFI</code>, <code>SUN</code>, <code>MOON</code>, <code>PALETTE</code></li></ul>", "toc": [{"title": "1. Light & Dark Theme Modes (ui.ThemeMode)", "id": "1-light-dark-theme-modes-ui-thememode"}, {"title": "2. The 8 Built-In ui.Accent Palettes", "id": "2-the-8-built-in-ui-accent-palettes"}, {"title": "3. Semantic ui.Tones (Badges, Alerts, Toasts, Kanban, Gantt)", "id": "3-semantic-ui-tones-badges-alerts-toasts-kanban-gantt"}, {"title": "4. Custom Brand Colors, Live Token Overrides & Perceptual OKLCH", "id": "4-custom-brand-colors-live-token-overrides-perceptual-oklch"}, {"title": "5. Typography, Custom .ttf Fonts & International Fallback", "id": "5-typography-custom-ttf-fonts-international-fallback"}, {"title": "6. Icons (ui.Icon)", "id": "6-icons-ui-icon"}]}, {"slug": "concurrency-and-async", "title": "Concurrency & Asyncio", "group": "Core Guides", "source": "docs/concurrency-and-async.md", "html": "<h1 id=\"concurrency-multithreading-asyncio-networking\">Concurrency, Multithreading, <code>asyncio</code>, &amp; Networking</h1>\n<p>Desktop GUIs freeze the moment you run a slow HTTP request, SQLite query, or LLM stream on the UI thread.</p>\n<p><code>nexa</code> is engineered from the C99 layer up for responsive, zero-CPU-idle concurrency:</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Every native C call releases Python&#x27;s GIL</strong>, so background Python threads run in parallel during layout and software rasterization.</li><li>**Cross-thread OS wakeup (<code>app.wake()</code>)<strong>: When your app is idle, it sleeps inside the OS event queue at </strong>0% CPU**. Calling <code>app.wake()</code> from <em>any</em> thread writes to a wakeup pipe (<code>X11</code>), posts <code>WM_NULL</code> (<code>Win32</code>), or posts an <code>NSEvent</code> (<code>Cocoa</code>) to render a new frame immediately.</li><li>**UI-thread callback marshaling (<code>app.call_soon_threadsafe(fn)</code>)**: Schedules state mutations to execute cleanly on the UI thread right before the next frame—eliminating race conditions without manual locks!</li></ol>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"pattern-1-backgroundrunner-threads-streaming-http-json\">Pattern 1: <code>BackgroundRunner</code> (Threads, Streaming &amp; HTTP JSON)</h2>\n<p><code>ui.BackgroundRunner.for_app(app)</code> (or <code>self.runner</code> inside any OOP <code>ui.Application</code>) manages a bounded pool of daemon threads and delivers <code>on_done</code>, <code>on_item</code>, and <code>on_error</code> callbacks <strong>on the UI thread</strong>, waking the window automatically.</p>\n<h3 id=\"complete-runnable-example-async-job-token-streaming\">Complete Runnable Example: Async Job + Token Streaming</h3>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> time\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">from</span> typing <span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">Iterator</span>\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> main() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    app = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">App</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Background Workers&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">680</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">440</span>, theme=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>, accent=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">VIOLET</span>)\n    runner = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BackgroundRunner</span>.for_app(app, max_workers=<span class=\"tok-num\">4</span>)\n\n    result_text = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Click a button to start background work.&quot;</span>\n    stream_buf = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>\n    job_handle: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TaskHandle</span>[str] | <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span> = <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>\n    stream_handle: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">TaskHandle</span>[<span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>] | <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span> = <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> compute_report() -&gt; str:\n        time.sleep(<span class=\"tok-num\">0.4</span>)  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Runs off-thread; UI stays silky smooth at 60fps!</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Compiled 42 modules in 0.40s&quot;</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> token_generator() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-cls\">Iterator</span>[str]:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> word <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> [<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Streaming&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;tokens&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;safely&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;onto&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;the&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;UI&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;thread!&quot;</span>]:\n            time.sleep(<span class=\"tok-num\">0.06</span>)\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">yield</span> word + <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot; &quot;</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">nonlocal</span> result_text, stream_buf, job_handle, stream_handle\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n            ctx.heading(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Non-Blocking Background Runner&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.row(gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, align=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Align</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">CENTER</span>):\n                <span class=\"tok-com\"># TaskHandle.button_status maps PENDING/RUNNING/DONE/FAILED -&gt; StatusButton states!</span>\n                btn_state = job_handle.button_status <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> job_handle <span class=\"tok-kw\">else</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Status</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">IDLE</span>\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.status_button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Run Background Job&quot;</span>, btn_state, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PLAY</span>):\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> _on_done(msg: str) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n                        <span class=\"tok-kw\">nonlocal</span> result_text\n                        result_text = msg\n                    job_handle = runner.submit(compute_report, on_done=_on_done)\n\n                streaming = stream_handle is <span class=\"tok-kw\">not</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">and</span> stream_handle.running\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">not</span> streaming:\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Stream Tokens&quot;</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SPARKLES</span>):\n                        stream_buf = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>\n                        <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> _on_tok(tok: str) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n                            <span class=\"tok-kw\">nonlocal</span> stream_buf\n                            stream_buf += tok\n                        stream_handle = runner.stream(token_generator, on_item=_on_tok)\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">else</span>:\n                    <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Stop Stream&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DANGER</span>, icon=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Icon</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">X</span>):\n                        stream_handle.cancel()\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">8</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n                ctx.secondary(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Job Result&quot;</span>)\n                ctx.text(result_text)\n\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.card(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">8</span>, width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>):\n                ctx.secondary(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Live Token Stream&quot;</span>)\n                ctx.text(stream_buf <span class=\"tok-kw\">or</span> <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Idle...&quot;</span>)\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">try</span>:\n        app.run(draw)\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">finally</span>:\n        runner.close()\n        app.close()\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    main()</code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"built-in-zero-dependency-http-helpers-fetch-json-fetch-bytes\">Built-in Zero-Dependency HTTP Helpers (<code>fetch_json</code> &amp; <code>fetch_bytes</code>)</h3>\n<p>Need to call a REST API without pulling in third-party packages? <code>BackgroundRunner</code> includes stdlib <code>urllib</code>-backed <code>fetch_json</code> and <code>fetch_bytes</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>handle = runner.fetch_json(\n    <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;https://api.example.com/v1/items&quot;</span>,\n    method=<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;POST&quot;</span>,\n    payload={<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;limit&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-num\">25</span>},\n    headers={<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Authorization&quot;</span>: <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Bearer ...&quot;</span>},\n    timeout=<span class=\"tok-num\">10.0</span>,\n    on_done=<span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> data: state.update({<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;items&quot;</span>: data}),\n    on_error=<span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> err: ctx.toast(str(err), tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DANGER</span>),\n)</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"pattern-2-producer-consumer-channel-t-thread-safe-logbuffer\">Pattern 2: Producer-Consumer <code>Channel[T]</code> &amp; Thread-Safe <code>LogBuffer</code></h2>\n<p>When a long-lived background thread (e.g., a WebSocket listener, serial port reader, or file watcher) emits high-frequency events:</p>\n<ul><li>**<code>ui.Channel(maxsize=256, wake=app.wake)</code>**: Thread-safe MPSC queue. Background threads call <code>channel.send(item)</code> (or non-blocking <code>channel.try_send(item)</code>), and your <code>draw()</code> function drains all queued items in one fast batch via <code>for msg in channel.drain():</code>.</li><li>**<code>ui.LogBuffer(max_lines=4096)</code>**: C-heap ring buffer protected by a lightweight lock. Any thread can call <code>log.info(...)</code>, <code>log.warn(...)</code>, <code>log.error(...)</code> directly while <code>ctx.log_view(&quot;console&quot;, log)</code> renders filterable, auto-scrolling logs at 60fps!</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"pattern-3-cooperative-single-thread-asyncio-await-app-run-async\">Pattern 3: Cooperative Single-Thread <code>asyncio</code> (<code>await app.run_async(...)</code>)</h2>\n<p>Already using <code>httpx.AsyncClient</code>, <code>aiohttp</code>, <code>websockets</code>, or <code>asyncio.StreamReader</code>? Run <code>nexa</code> **cooperatively inside your existing <code>asyncio</code> event loop**—zero extra threads, zero locks!</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> asyncio\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">async</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> main() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    app = ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">App</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Asyncio Cooperative UI&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">560</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">320</span>, theme=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>, accent=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Accent</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BLUE</span>)\n    ticks = <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>\n    status = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Waiting for async task...&quot;</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">async</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> background_poller() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">nonlocal</span> ticks, status\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">while</span> <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>:\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">await</span> asyncio.sleep(<span class=\"tok-num\">0.5</span>)\n            ticks += <span class=\"tok-num\">1</span>\n            status = f<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Async heartbeat #{ticks}&quot;</span>\n            app.wake()  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Triggers an immediate UI frame!</span>\n\n    poller = asyncio.create_task(background_poller())\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n            ctx.heading(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Cooperative asyncio + nexa&quot;</span>, level=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)\n            ctx.badge(status, tone=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Tone</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">INFO</span>, dot=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>)\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">try</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">await</span> app.run_async(draw)\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">finally</span>:\n        poller.cancel()\n        app.close()\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    asyncio.run(main())</code></pre></div>\n<p>OOP <code>ui.Application</code> subclasses also support <code>await MyApp().run_async()</code> out of the box!</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"pattern-4-dedicated-thread-asyncbridge\">Pattern 4: Dedicated-Thread <code>AsyncBridge</code></h2>\n<p>If your main thread runs synchronous <code>app.run(draw)</code> (ensuring the OS window loop never waits on a slow coroutine) while third-party <code>async def</code> coroutines or async generators run on a dedicated background <code>asyncio</code> event loop thread, use <code>nexa.aio.AsyncBridge</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">from</span> nexa.aio <span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> <span class=\"tok-cls\">AsyncBridge</span>\n\nbridge = <span class=\"tok-cls\">AsyncBridge</span>.for_app(app)  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Or `self.async_bridge` on any `ui.Application`!</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># Schedule a coroutine on the background asyncio loop; `on_done` runs on the UI thread:</span>\nhandle = bridge.spawn(fetch_user_profile(user_id), on_done=<span class=\"tok-kw\">lambda</span> prof: set_profile(prof))\n\n<span class=\"tok-com\"># Stream an async generator (`async for chunk in ...`) onto the UI thread:</span>\nstream_h = bridge.stream(llm_client.stream_chat(messages), on_item=chunks.append)</code></pre></div>", "toc": [{"title": "Pattern 1: BackgroundRunner (Threads, Streaming & HTTP JSON)", "id": "pattern-1-backgroundrunner-threads-streaming-http-json"}, {"title": "Pattern 2: Producer-Consumer Channel[T] & Thread-Safe LogBuffer", "id": "pattern-2-producer-consumer-channel-t-thread-safe-logbuffer"}, {"title": "Pattern 3: Cooperative Single-Thread asyncio (await app.run_async(...))", "id": "pattern-3-cooperative-single-thread-asyncio-await-app-run-async"}, {"title": "Pattern 4: Dedicated-Thread AsyncBridge", "id": "pattern-4-dedicated-thread-asyncbridge"}]}, {"slug": "components-reference", "title": "150+ Components Reference", "group": "API Reference", "source": "docs/components-reference.md", "html": "<h1 id=\"complete-component-reference-150-widgets-across-19-domains\">Complete Component Reference (150+ Widgets Across 19 Domains)</h1>\n<p>Every widget method below is available <strong>both</strong> on <code>ctx: ui.UI</code> (<code>ctx.button(...)</code>) <strong>and</strong> as a top-level function when inside an active frame (<code>import nexa as ui; ui.button(...)</code>).</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"1-layout-containers-nexa-widgets-layout\">1. Layout &amp; Containers (<code>nexa.widgets.layout</code>)</h2>\n<p>All layout scopes are <strong>unconditional</strong> (<code>with ui.row(...):</code> always enters).</p>\n<ul><li>**<code>box(*, id=None, dir=Direction.COLUMN, width=None, height=None, min_width=0, max_width=0, min_height=0, max_height=0, pad=0, pad_x=0, pad_y=0, pad_top=0, pad_right=0, pad_bottom=0, pad_left=0, gap=0, columns=0, min_column_width=0, wrap=False, align=Align.STRETCH, justify=Justify.START, bg=None, border_color=None, border=0, radius=0, corners=None, elevation=Elevation.NONE, scroll_x=False, scroll_y=False, clip=False, opacity=0)</code>**</li><li>**<code>row(**box_kwargs)</code>** — Horizontal flex container (<code>wrap=True</code> enables multi-line flex wrap).</li><li>**<code>column(**box_kwargs)</code>** — Vertical flex container.</li><li>**<code>stack(**box_kwargs)</code>** — Overlapping Z-stack container (<code>Direction.STACK</code>).</li><li>**<code>grid(*, columns=0, min_column_width=0, gap=12, **box_kwargs)</code>** — Responsive CSS-Grid-like multi-column container.</li><li>**<code>card(*, id=None, width=None, height=None, pad=0, pad_x=0, pad_y=0, gap=0, dir=Direction.COLUMN, align=Align.STRETCH, wrap=False, hoverable=False, selected=False, muted=False)</code>** -&gt; <code>CardScope</code> (<code>card.clicked</code> is <code>True</code> when <code>hoverable=True</code> card is clicked).</li><li>**<code>scroll(id, *, width=None, height=None, pad=0, pad_x=0, pad_y=0, gap=0, horizontal=False, sticky_bottom=False, fade_edges=False)</code><strong> + </strong><code>scroll_to(id, y)</code>**.</li><li>**<code>split(id, ratio, *, vertical=False, min_first=120, min_second=120, width=None, height=None)</code>** -&gt; <code>SplitScope</code> (call <code>sp.next()</code> between pane 1 and pane 2; read updated <code>sp.ratio</code>).</li><li>**<code>spacer()</code><strong> | </strong><code>gap(px)</code><strong> | </strong><code>separator()</code>**</li><li>**<code>id_scope(key: str | int)</code><strong> | </strong><code>disabled_scope(disabled: bool = True)</code>**</li><li>Queries: **<code>make_id(s)</code><strong>, </strong><code>last_id</code><strong>, </strong><code>last_hovered</code><strong>, </strong><code>last_rect</code><strong>, </strong><code>get_rect(id)</code><strong>, </strong><code>is_disabled</code>**.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"2-text-typography-nexa-widgets-text\">2. Text &amp; Typography (<code>nexa.widgets.text</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>text(content, *, font=FontRole.BODY, size=0, color=None, align=TextAlign.LEFT, max_lines=0, selectable=False, strikethrough=False, underline=False, nowrap=False, width=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>heading(content, level=2)</code>** (<code>level</code> in <code>1..4</code>)</li><li>**<code>label(content)</code><strong> | </strong><code>secondary(content)</code><strong> | </strong><code>muted(content)</code>**</li><li>**<code>code(content)</code>** — Inline monospace pill (<code>Geist Mono</code>).</li><li>**<code>kbd(shortcut)</code>** — Styled keycap chord (<code>&quot;Ctrl K&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;Shift Tab&quot;</code>).</li><li>**<code>link(label, **opts) -&gt; bool</code>** — Clickable underlined link.</li><li>**<code>icon(glyph, size=16.0, color=None)</code>** — Renders any <code>ui.Icon.*</code> glyph.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"3-buttons-actions-nexa-widgets-actions\">3. Buttons &amp; Actions (<code>nexa.widgets.actions</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>button(label, *, variant=ButtonVariant.DEFAULT, size=ControlSize.MD, icon=None, icon_right=None, disabled=False, loading=False, full_width=False, selected=False, tooltip=None, shortcut=None, width=None, color=None) -&gt; bool</code>**<ul><li><code>ButtonVariant</code>: <code>DEFAULT</code>, <code>PRIMARY</code>, <code>SECONDARY</code>, <code>OUTLINE</code>, <code>GHOST</code>, <code>DANGER</code>, <code>LINK</code>.</li></ul></li><li>**<code>icon_button(icon, **button_opts) -&gt; bool</code>**</li><li>**<code>button_group()</code>** — Unconditional scope joining child buttons into a segmented bar.</li><li>**<code>copy_button(id, text_to_copy, *, label=None, copied_label=&quot;Copied&quot;, size=ControlSize.MD, ghost=False) -&gt; bool</code>**</li><li>**<code>hold_button(label, *, duration=1.2, variant=ButtonVariant.DANGER, icon=None, size=ControlSize.MD, disabled=False) -&gt; bool</code>** — Press-and-hold progress button for destructive/financial actions.</li><li>**<code>confirm_button(label, *, confirm_label=&quot;Click to confirm&quot;, icon=None, variant=ButtonVariant.SECONDARY, size=ControlSize.MD, timeout=3.0, disabled=False) -&gt; bool</code>** — Two-step morphing confirmation button.</li><li>**<code>status_button(label, status: Status, *, busy_label=None, success_label=&quot;Done&quot;, error_label=&quot;Failed&quot;, variant=ButtonVariant.PRIMARY, size=ControlSize.MD, icon=None) -&gt; bool</code>** (<code>Status</code>: <code>IDLE</code>, <code>BUSY</code>, <code>SUCCESS</code>, <code>ERROR</code>).</li><li>**<code>split_button(label, menu_items, *, variant=ButtonVariant.PRIMARY, size=ControlSize.MD, icon=None, disabled=False) -&gt; int</code>** (<code>0</code> = main click, <code>1..N</code> = dropdown item <code>0..N-1</code>, <code>-1</code> = none).</li><li>**<code>segmented(id, labels, selected: int, *, icons=None, size=ControlSize.MD, full_width=False) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>toggle_group(id, labels, values: Sequence[bool], *, icons=None, icon_only=False, exclusive=False, size=ControlSize.MD) -&gt; list[bool]</code>**</li><li>**<code>reactions(id, items: Sequence[Reaction]) -&gt; tuple[list[Reaction], int]</code>**</li><li>**<code>speed_dial(id, actions: Sequence[SpeedAction], *, icon=None, place=Placement.TOP) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>swipe_item(id, *, left=(), right=())</code>** -&gt; <code>SwipeItemScope</code> (<code>sw.action</code>: <code>0..99</code> left, <code>100+</code> right, <code>-1</code> none).</li><li>**<code>command_palette(open: bool, commands: Sequence[Command], *, placeholder=&quot;Type a command...&quot;) -&gt; tuple[bool, int]</code>**</li><li>**<code>theme_switcher(mode: int) -&gt; int</code><strong> | </strong><code>theme_toggle() -&gt; bool</code>**</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"4-selection-controls-nexa-widgets-selection\">4. Selection Controls (<code>nexa.widgets.selection</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>checkbox(label, checked: bool, *, description=None, indeterminate=False, disabled=False) -&gt; bool</code>**</li><li>**<code>switch(label, on: bool, *, description=None, disabled=False) -&gt; bool</code>**</li><li>**<code>radio(label, current: int, option_value: int) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>radio_group(id, labels, selected: int, *, descriptions=None, disabled=False) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>radio_cards(id, choices: Sequence[Choice], selected: int, *, columns=0, disabled=False) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>slider(label, value: float, min_val=0.0, max_val=1.0, *, step=0.0, format=None, show_value=False, ticks=False, disabled=False, width=None) -&gt; float</code>**</li><li>**<code>range_slider(label, low: float, high: float, min_val=0.0, max_val=1.0, **opts) -&gt; tuple[float, float]</code>**</li><li>**<code>rating(id, value: int, max_stars=5, *, read_only=False, size=0) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>chip(label, active: bool = False, *, icon=None, removable=False, tone=Tone.NEUTRAL, size=ControlSize.MD) -&gt; bool | tuple[bool, bool]</code>**</li><li>**<code>control_tile(label, on: bool, *, detail=None, icon=None, width=None, disabled=False) -&gt; bool</code>**</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"5-text-specialized-inputs-nexa-widgets-inputs\">5. Text &amp; Specialized Inputs (<code>nexa.widgets.inputs</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>input(id, value: str, *, max_bytes=512, label=None, placeholder=None, icon=None, hint=None, error=None, password=False, disabled=False, clearable=False, autofocus=False, read_only=False, size=ControlSize.MD, width=None, prefix=None, suffix=None) -&gt; str</code>**</li><li>**<code>search(id, value: str, *, placeholder=&quot;Search...&quot;, size=ControlSize.MD, width=None) -&gt; str</code>**</li><li>**<code>textarea(id, value: str, *, max_bytes=8192, height=120.0 | ui.FILL, **input_opts) -&gt; str</code>**</li><li>**<code>number(id, value: float, min_val=0.0, max_val=100.0, *, step=1.0, decimals=0, label=None, prefix=None, suffix=None, width=None) -&gt; float</code>**</li><li>**<code>scrub(label, value: float, min_val=-1e9, max_val=1e9, *, step=1.0, decimals=2, suffix=None, width=None) -&gt; float</code>**</li><li>**<code>money_input(id, cents_or_amount: float, *, symbol=&quot;$&quot;, code=&quot;USD&quot;, decimals=2, allow_negative=False, label=None, width=None) -&gt; float</code>**</li><li>**<code>inline_edit(id, value: str, *, font=FontRole.BODY, size=0, placeholder=&quot;Untitled&quot;, width=None) -&gt; str</code>**</li><li>**<code>tag_input(id, tags: list[str] | str, *, label=None, placeholder=&quot;Add tag...&quot;, max_tags=0, width=None) -&gt; list[str] | str</code>**</li><li>**<code>otp_input(id, code: str, digits=6, *, masked=False) -&gt; tuple[str, bool]</code>** (<code>(code, completed)</code>)</li><li>**<code>password_strength(password: str, *, show_rules=True) -&gt; int</code>** (<code>0..4</code> score)</li><li>**<code>shortcut_recorder(id, combo: KeyCombo, *, clearable=True, width=None) -&gt; KeyCombo</code>**</li><li>**<code>signature_pad(id, *, width=None, height=160.0, pen_color=None, stroke_width=2.2, label=None) -&gt; bool</code>** (+ <code>signature_strokes(id)</code>, <code>signature_clear(id)</code>)</li><li>**<code>dropzone(id, *, title=None, description=None, icon=None, accept=None, height=0, width=None, compact=False) -&gt; tuple[list[str], bool]</code>** (<code>(accepted_paths, browse_clicked)</code>)</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"6-pickers-nexa-widgets-pickers\">6. Pickers (<code>nexa.widgets.pickers</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>select(id, options, selected: int, *, label=None, placeholder=None, width=None, size=ControlSize.MD) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>combobox(id, options, selected: int, *, label=None, placeholder=&quot;Search...&quot;, width=None) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>multi_select(id, options, selected: Sequence[bool], *, label=None, placeholder=&quot;Select...&quot;, width=None) -&gt; list[bool]</code>**</li><li>**<code>calendar(id, date: Date, *, min_date=None, max_date=None) -&gt; Date</code>**</li><li>**<code>date_picker(id, date: Date, *, label=None, width=None, min_date=None, max_date=None) -&gt; Date</code>**</li><li>**<code>range_calendar(id, date_range: DateRange, *, months=2) -&gt; DateRange</code>**</li><li>**<code>date_range_picker(id, date_range: DateRange, *, label=None, width=None, months=2) -&gt; DateRange</code>**</li><li>**<code>time_picker(id, hour: int, minute: int, *, use_24h=True, step_minutes=1, label=None, width=None) -&gt; tuple[int, int]</code>**</li><li>**<code>time_dial(id, hour: int, minute: int, *, use_24h=True, size=200.0) -&gt; tuple[int, int]</code>**</li><li>**<code>wheel_picker(id, items, selected: int, *, visible_rows=5, loop=False, width=None) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>ruler_slider(label, value: float, min_val: float, max_val: float, *, step=1.0, major_every=10, unit=None, width=None) -&gt; float</code>**</li><li>**<code>histogram_slider(label, bins, low: float, high: float, min_val: float, max_val: float, *, height=56.0, width=None) -&gt; tuple[float, float]</code>**</li><li>**<code>color_picker(id, color: ColorLike, *, alpha=False, swatches=True, hex_input=True, popover=False, width=None) -&gt; Color</code>**</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"7-navigation-nexa-widgets-navigation\">7. Navigation (<code>nexa.widgets.navigation</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>tabs(id, labels, selected: int, *, variant=TabsVariant.LINE, icons=None, badges=None) -&gt; int</code>** (<code>TabsVariant</code>: <code>LINE</code>, <code>PILL</code>, <code>ENCLOSED</code>)</li><li>**<code>nav_section(title)</code><strong> | </strong><code>nav_item(label, *, icon=None, badge=None, selected=False, disabled=False, group=None) -&gt; bool</code>**</li><li>**<code>breadcrumb(items, *, separator=None) -&gt; int</code>** (returns clicked crumb index or <code>-1</code>)</li><li>**<code>pagination(id, page: int, page_count: int, *, siblings=1) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>stepper(steps, current: int, *, clickable=True) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>tab_bar(id, items: Sequence[TabBarItem], selected: int, *, pill=False, icon_only=False, width=None) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>dock(id, *, magnify=0.45, base_size=44.0)</code><strong> + </strong><code>dock_item(icon, label, *, running=False, attention=False, badge=0) -&gt; bool</code><strong> + </strong><code>dock_separator()</code>**</li><li>**<code>toc(id, scroll_id, headings, *, title=&quot;On this page&quot;, width=200.0) -&gt; int</code><strong> + </strong><code>toc_anchor(scroll_id, index)</code>**</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"8-overlays-menus-disclosure-nexa-widgets-overlays\">8. Overlays, Menus &amp; Disclosure (<code>nexa.widgets.overlays</code>)</h2>\n<p>All popup/overlay scopes are <strong>conditional</strong>—always write <code>with ui.dialog(...) as d: if d: ...</code>!</p>\n<ul><li>**<code>tooltip(text)</code>** — Attaches a hover tooltip to the immediately preceding widget.</li><li>**<code>popover(id, *, place=Placement.BOTTOM_START, width=0)</code>** (<code>popover_open(id)</code>, <code>popover_is_open(id)</code>, <code>popover_close()</code>)</li><li>**<code>hover_card(id, *, width=280.0, place=Placement.BOTTOM)</code>**</li><li>**<code>confirm_popover(id, *, title=&quot;Are you sure?&quot;, description=None, confirm_label=&quot;Confirm&quot;, cancel_label=&quot;Cancel&quot;, danger=False) -&gt; bool</code>** (<code>confirm_popover_open(id)</code> opens it on the anchor widget)</li><li>**<code>menu(label, *, icon=None, variant=ButtonVariant.OUTLINE, size=ControlSize.MD)</code><strong> + </strong><code>context_menu(id)</code><strong> + </strong><code>user_menu(name, *, detail=None, avatar_tex=0, status=None, compact=False)</code>**<ul><li>Inside menus: **<code>menu_item(label, *, icon=None, shortcut=None, disabled=False, danger=False, checked=False) -&gt; bool</code><strong>, </strong><code>menu_separator()</code><strong>, </strong><code>menu_label(text)</code>**.</li></ul></li><li>**<code>dialog(title, open: bool, *, description=None, width=440.0, dismissible=True, close_button=True)</code>** -&gt; <code>BoolStateScope</code> (<code>dlg.open</code>) + **<code>dialog_footer()</code>**.</li><li>**<code>sheet(title, open: bool, *, description=None, side=Side.RIGHT, size=380.0, modal=True)</code>** -&gt; <code>BoolStateScope</code> (<code>sh.open</code>).</li><li>**<code>accordion(title, expanded: bool, *, subtitle=None, icon=None)</code>** -&gt; <code>BoolStateScope</code> (<code>acc.open</code>).</li><li>**<code>expandable_card(title, expanded: bool, *, subtitle=None, icon=None, badge=None, width=None)</code>** -&gt; <code>BoolStateScope</code>.</li><li>**<code>expandable_text(id, text, *, lines=3, more_label=&quot;Show more&quot;, less_label=&quot;Show less&quot;)</code>**</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"9-feedback-status-badges-nexa-widgets-feedback\">9. Feedback, Status &amp; Badges (<code>nexa.widgets.feedback</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>toast(title, *, description=None, tone=Tone.NEUTRAL, duration=4.0, action=None, dismissible=True) -&gt; int</code>** (+ <code>toast_action_clicked(h)</code>, <code>toast_dismiss(h)</code>)</li><li>**<code>alert(title, *, description=None, tone=Tone.INFO, icon=None, action=None, dismissible=False) -&gt; tuple[bool, bool]</code>**</li><li>**<code>banner(title, open: bool = True, *, action=None, tone=Tone.INFO, icon=None, dismissible=True) -&gt; tuple[bool, bool]</code>**</li><li>**<code>progress(value: float, *, indeterminate=False, label=None, show_value=False, tone=Tone.ACCENT, height=0, width=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>progress_ring(label, value: float, *, size=64.0, thickness=6.0, sublabel=None, color=None, indeterminate=False)</code>**</li><li>**<code>spinner(size=18.0)</code><strong> | </strong><code>loader(*, style=LoaderStyle.SPINNER, size=24.0, label=None, color=None)</code><strong> | </strong><code>skeleton(width, height, *, circle=False)</code>**</li><li>**<code>badge(text, *, tone=Tone.NEUTRAL, outline=False, dot=False, icon=None, size=ControlSize.MD)</code>**</li><li>**<code>avatar(name, *, image=0, size=36.0, circle=True, status=None)</code><strong> | </strong><code>avatar_group(names, *, max_visible=4, size=32.0)</code><strong> | </strong><code>avatar_upload(id, name, image=0, *, size=72.0) -&gt; tuple[int, bool]</code>**</li><li>**<code>empty_state(title, *, description=None, icon=None, action=None) -&gt; bool</code>**</li><li>**<code>metric(label, value, *, delta=None, delta_text=None, hint=None, spark=None, lower_is_better=False, width=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>meter(label, used: float, total: float, unit=&quot;&quot;, *, warn_at=0.75, crit_at=0.90, width=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>countdown(id, remaining_seconds: float, *, label=None, show_days=False, compact=False) -&gt; bool</code>**</li><li>**<code>checklist(id, steps: Sequence[CheckStep], *, title=None, dismissible=False, width=None) -&gt; tuple[int, bool]</code>**</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"10-data-virtual-lists-tables-grids-code-nexa-widgets-data\">10. Data, Virtual Lists, Tables, Grids &amp; Code (<code>nexa.widgets.data</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>tree(label, expanded=False, *, icon=None, badge=None, leaf=False, selected=False)</code>** -&gt; <code>TreeScope</code> (<code>if tr:</code> for children; <code>tr.expanded</code>, <code>tr.clicked</code>).</li><li>**<code>list_item(title, *, subtitle=None, trailing=None, icon=None, avatar=None, badge=None, badge_tone=Tone.NEUTRAL, chevron=False, selected=False, active=False) -&gt; bool</code>**</li><li>**<code>virtual_list(id, row_count: int, row_height: float, height: SizeLike = None)</code>** -&gt; <code>VirtualListScope</code> (iterate <code>for i in vl.indices:</code>—renders 1,000,000+ rows in O(visible)!).</li><li>**<code>reorder(id, order: Sequence[int], *, horizontal=False, gap=6.0, width=None)</code>** -&gt; <code>ReorderScope</code> (<code>with ro.item(pos): ...</code>; read <code>ro.order</code>).</li><li>**<code>timeline_item(title, *, description=None, time=None, icon=None, tone=Tone.ACCENT, last=False)</code>**</li><li>**<code>table(id, columns: Sequence[TableColumn], *, sort=None, height=None, striped=False, compact=False, selectable=False)</code>** -&gt; <code>TableScope</code> (<code>if tbl:</code>; <code>tbl.row(selected=...) -&gt; bool</code>, <code>tbl.cell()</code>, <code>tbl.cell_text(s)</code>, <code>tbl.sort</code>).</li><li>**<code>data_grid(id, columns: Sequence[GridColumn], row_count: int, *, width=None, height=None, row_height=0, selected=None, sort=None, striped=False, borderless=False, cursor=0)</code>** -&gt; <code>DataGridScope</code> (<code>if dg:</code>; <code>for r in dg.rows:</code>, <code>dg.row(r)</code>, <code>dg.cell_text(s)</code>, <code>dg.edit(val)</code>, <code>dg.selected</code>, <code>dg.sort</code>, <code>dg.cursor</code>).</li><li>**<code>filter_bar(id, fields: Sequence[FilterField], masks: Sequence[int], search: str = &quot;&quot;, *, clearable=True, width=None) -&gt; tuple[list[int], str]</code>**</li><li>**<code>code_block(id, source, *, lang=&quot;python&quot;, line_numbers=True, copyable=True, wrap=False, highlight_line=0, max_height=0, filename=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>json_view(id, json_str, *, default_open_depth=2, max_height=0, copyable=True) -&gt; bool</code>**</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"11-charts-data-visualization-nexa-widgets-charts\">11. Charts &amp; Data Visualization (<code>nexa.widgets.charts</code>)</h2>\n<ul><li>**<code>line_chart(id, series: Sequence[Series], *, labels=None, height=200.0, width=None, smooth=False, area=False, show_points=False, show_grid=True, show_legend=False, y_min=0, y_max=0, reference_y=None, reference_label=None, y_format=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>bar_chart(id, series: Sequence[Series], *, labels=None, stacked=False, horizontal=False, height=200.0, width=None, **opts)</code>**</li><li>**<code>donut_chart(id, values, labels=None, *, colors=None, height=180.0, width=None, thickness=0.32, show_legend=True, center_label=None, format=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>sparkline(values, *, width=100.0, height=28.0, color=None, area=True)</code>**</li><li>**<code>gauge(label, value: float, *, min_val=0.0, max_val=1.0, sublabel=None, size=120.0, color=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>heatmap(id, values, rows: int, cols: int, *, row_labels=None, col_labels=None, color=None, show_values=False, format=None, cell_size=0, width=None) -&gt; tuple[int, int]</code>**</li><li>**<code>calendar_heatmap(id, start_date: Date, daily_values, *, color=None, unit=&quot;contributions&quot;, cell_size=0) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>treemap(id, items: Sequence[VizItem], *, width=None, height=240.0, format=None) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>radar_chart(id, series: Sequence[Series], axes_labels, *, max_val=0, size=220.0, show_legend=False)</code>**</li><li>**<code>funnel(id, stages: Sequence[VizItem], *, width=None, height=220.0, format=None) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>sankey(id, nodes: Sequence[str], links: Sequence[SankeyLink], *, width=None, height=260.0, format=None, node_width=0) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>waffle(id, parts: Sequence[VizItem], *, rows=10, cols=10, title=None, cell_size=0, legend=True)</code>**</li><li>**<code>split_bar(id, parts: Sequence[VizItem], *, height=10.0, width=None, legend=True, format=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>bar_list(id, items: Sequence[VizItem], *, format=None, show_percent=False, color=None, width=None) -&gt; int</code>**</li><li>**<code>activity_rings(id, rings: Sequence[VizItem], *, size=120.0, legend=False, center_text=None, sublabel=None)</code>**</li><li>**<code>scatter_chart(id, series: Sequence[ScatterSeries], *, width=None, height=220.0, x_label=None, y_label=None, x_format=None, y_format=None, no_legend=False) -&gt; tuple[int, int]</code>**</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"12-19-planning-ai-social-media-motion-chrome-tools-node-canvas\">12–19. Planning, AI, Social, Media, Motion, Chrome, Tools &amp; Node/Canvas</h2>\n<ul><li>**Planning (<code>nexa.widgets.planning</code>)**:<ul><li><code>kanban(id)</code> -&gt; <code>KanbanScope</code> (<code>board.column(title, count, dot=..., width=...)</code>, <code>board.card(id)</code>, <code>board.move</code>)</li><li><code>week_calendar(id, week_start: Date, events: Sequence[CalEvent], **opts) -&gt; tuple[list[CalEvent], int]</code></li><li><code>gantt(id, tasks: Sequence[GanttTask], origin: Date, days: int, **opts) -&gt; tuple[list[GanttTask], int]</code></li></ul></li><li>**AI &amp; Agents (<code>nexa.widgets.ai</code>)**:<ul><li><code>reasoning(id, *, thinking=False, seconds=0, title=None, default_open=False)</code></li><li><code>tool_call(id, name, *, status=TaskStatus.DONE, detail=None, input_text=None, output_text=None, seconds=0)</code></li><li><code>agent_plan(id, steps: Sequence[PlanStep], *, title=None, width=None)</code> | <code>agent_status(label, *, detail=None, status=TaskStatus.RUNNING, seconds=0)</code></li><li><code>source_list(id, sources: Sequence[Source], *, compact=False) -&gt; int</code> | <code>citation(number: int, source: Source) -&gt; bool</code></li><li><code>context_meter(id, used: int, limit: int, *, unit=&quot;tokens&quot;, parts=None, cost_usd=-1)</code></li><li><code>response_actions(id, *, copy_text=None, vote=0, regenerate=True, edit=False, branch=False, more=False) -&gt; tuple[ResponseFlags, int]</code></li><li><code>prompt_suggestions(id, items: Sequence[PromptSuggestion], *, columns=2, width=None) -&gt; int</code></li><li><code>model_picker(id, models: Sequence[Model], selected: int, *, ghost=False, size=ControlSize.SM) -&gt; int</code></li><li><code>chat_composer(id, text: str, *, placeholder=..., busy=False, attachments=None, models=None, model=0, **opts) -&gt; ComposerResult</code></li><li><code>voice_orb(id, state=VoiceState.IDLE, level=0.0, *, size=72.0, color=None) -&gt; bool</code></li></ul></li><li>**Social (<code>nexa.widgets.social</code>)**: <code>chat_message</code>, <code>chat_divider</code>, <code>typing_indicator</code>, <code>comment</code>, <code>presence</code>.</li><li>**Media (<code>nexa.widgets.media</code>)**: <code>image_load</code>, <code>image_load_bytes</code>, <code>image_create</code>, <code>image_destroy</code>, <code>image</code>, <code>carousel</code>, <code>image_compare</code>, <code>card_stack</code>, <code>waveform</code>, <code>now_playing</code>, <code>counter</code>, <code>ticker</code>.</li><li>**Motion (<code>nexa.widgets.motion</code>)**: <code>shimmer_text</code>, <code>typewriter</code>, <code>text_reveal</code>, <code>word_rotate</code>, <code>number_roll</code>, <code>gradient_text</code>, <code>spotlight</code>, <code>animate</code>, <code>animate_spring</code>.</li><li>**Desktop Chrome (<code>nexa.widgets.chrome</code>)**: <code>menu_bar</code> + <code>menu_bar_menu</code>, <code>toolbar</code> + <code>toolbar_button</code> / <code>toolbar_toggle</code> / <code>toolbar_separator</code> / <code>toolbar_spacer</code>, <code>status_bar</code> + <code>status_bar_item</code> / <code>status_bar_text</code> / <code>status_bar_progress</code> / <code>status_bar_spacer</code>, <code>doc_tabs</code> (<code>DocTabsResult.apply_to(tabs)</code>).</li><li>**Developer Tools (<code>nexa.widgets.tools</code>)**: <code>inspector</code> + <code>inspector_group</code>, <code>prop_float</code>, <code>prop_int</code>, <code>prop_text</code>, <code>prop_bool</code>, <code>prop_enum</code>, <code>prop_color</code>, <code>prop_vec2/3/4</code>, <code>LogBuffer</code> + <code>log_view</code>.</li><li>**Node Editor &amp; Vector Canvas (<code>nexa.widgets.nodes_canvas</code>)**: <code>node_editor</code> (<code>ed.node</code>, <code>ed.input</code>, <code>ed.output</code>, <code>ed.content</code>, <code>ed.link</code>, <code>ed.created_links</code>, <code>ed.removed_links</code>), <code>canvas(id, w, h, paint_fn)</code>, <code>draw_rect</code>, <code>draw_rect_border</code>, <code>draw_rect_gradient</code>, <code>draw_line</code>, <code>draw_polyline</code>, <code>draw_polygon</code>, <code>draw_circle</code>, <code>draw_arc</code>, <code>draw_bezier</code>, <code>draw_text</code>, <code>draw_image</code>, <code>clip_scope</code>, <code>state_buffer</code>.</li></ul>", "toc": [{"title": "1. Layout & Containers (nexa.widgets.layout)", "id": "1-layout-containers-nexa-widgets-layout"}, {"title": "2. Text & Typography (nexa.widgets.text)", "id": "2-text-typography-nexa-widgets-text"}, {"title": "3. Buttons & Actions (nexa.widgets.actions)", "id": "3-buttons-actions-nexa-widgets-actions"}, {"title": "4. Selection Controls (nexa.widgets.selection)", "id": "4-selection-controls-nexa-widgets-selection"}, {"title": "5. Text & Specialized Inputs (nexa.widgets.inputs)", "id": "5-text-specialized-inputs-nexa-widgets-inputs"}, {"title": "6. Pickers (nexa.widgets.pickers)", "id": "6-pickers-nexa-widgets-pickers"}, {"title": "7. Navigation (nexa.widgets.navigation)", "id": "7-navigation-nexa-widgets-navigation"}, {"title": "8. Overlays, Menus & Disclosure (nexa.widgets.overlays)", "id": "8-overlays-menus-disclosure-nexa-widgets-overlays"}, {"title": "9. Feedback, Status & Badges (nexa.widgets.feedback)", "id": "9-feedback-status-badges-nexa-widgets-feedback"}, {"title": "10. Data, Virtual Lists, Tables, Grids & Code (nexa.widgets.data)", "id": "10-data-virtual-lists-tables-grids-code-nexa-widgets-data"}, {"title": "11. Charts & Data Visualization (nexa.widgets.charts)", "id": "11-charts-data-visualization-nexa-widgets-charts"}, {"title": "12–19. Planning, AI, Social, Media, Motion, Chrome, Tools & Node/Canvas", "id": "12-19-planning-ai-social-media-motion-chrome-tools-node-canvas"}]}, {"slug": "advanced-rendering-and-packaging", "title": "Canvas, GPU & Packaging", "group": "Advanced", "source": "docs/advanced-rendering-and-packaging.md", "html": "<h1 id=\"custom-canvas-headless-testing-custom-gpu-packaging\">Custom Canvas, Headless Testing, Custom GPU &amp; Packaging</h1>\n<p>Beyond its 150+ built-in components, <code>nexa</code> exposes every low-level primitive of the underlying C99 engine so you can build custom vector instruments, write deterministic CI tests, plug into Vulkan/Metal/Direct3D/<code>wgpu</code>, or ship tiny standalone binaries.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"1-custom-vector-canvas-persistent-state-buffer\">1. Custom Vector <code>canvas</code> &amp; Persistent <code>state_buffer</code></h2>\n<p>Reserve layout space with <code>ctx.canvas(id, width, height, paint_fn)</code>—<code>nexa</code> runs flexbox layout first, then invokes <code>paint_fn(ctx, rect)</code> with the resolved screen <code>Rect(x, y, w, h)</code> and returns a <code>CanvasResult</code> (<code>rect</code>, <code>mouse</code>, <code>hovered</code>, <code>pressed</code>, <code>clicked</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> math\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> main() -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> draw(ctx: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(width=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, height=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">20</span>, bg=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">BACKGROUND</span>):\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> paint_scope(c: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>, r: ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Rect</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"tok-kw\">None</span>:\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> c.clip_scope(r):\n                    c.draw_rect_gradient(r, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#0f172a&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#1e293b&quot;</span>, radius=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>)\n                    pts = [\n                        (r.x + (i / <span class=\"tok-num\">80.0</span>) * r.w, r.y + r.h * <span class=\"tok-num\">0.5</span> + math.sin(c.time * <span class=\"tok-num\">4.0</span> + i * <span class=\"tok-num\">0.2</span>) * (r.h * <span class=\"tok-num\">0.3</span>))\n                        <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> i <span class=\"tok-kw\">in</span> range(<span class=\"tok-num\">81</span>)\n                    ]\n                    c.draw_polyline(pts, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">Color</span>.hex(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#53dca6&quot;</span>), thickness=<span class=\"tok-num\">2.2</span>)\n                    c.draw_text(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Live SDF Oscilloscope&quot;</span>, (r.x + <span class=\"tok-num\">16</span>, r.y + <span class=\"tok-num\">14</span>), <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;#e2e8f0&quot;</span>, size=<span class=\"tok-num\">13</span>)\n\n            res = ctx.canvas(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;osc&quot;</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">FILL</span>, paint_scope)\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> res.hovered:\n                ctx.request_redraw()  <span class=\"tok-com\"># Animate continuously while hovered</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">App</span>(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Custom Canvas&quot;</span>, width=<span class=\"tok-num\">640</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">360</span>, theme=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ThemeMode</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">DARK</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> app:\n        app.run(draw)\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    main()</code></pre></div>\n<p>Need C-managed per-widget byte storage for a custom control? <code>mv = ctx.state_buffer(&quot;my_knob&quot;, 16)</code> returns a zero-initialized writable <code>memoryview</code> persisted in CUI&#x27;s widget state hash table (automatically garbage-collected if the widget stops rendering).</p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"2-automated-headless-ui-testing-png-snapshots\">2. Automated Headless UI Testing &amp; PNG Snapshots</h2>\n<p>You can test <strong>every click, keystroke, text edit, and file drop</strong> in <code>pytest</code> at thousands of frames per second without opening an OS window:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>python</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class=\"tok-kw\">import</span> nexa <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ui\n\n<span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> test_login_form(tmp_path):\n    <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">SoftwareRenderer</span>(threads=<span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> sw, ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">UI</span>(width=<span class=\"tok-num\">480</span>, height=<span class=\"tok-num\">320</span>, renderer=sw) <span class=\"tok-kw\">as</span> ctx:\n        username = <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;&quot;</span>\n        submitted = <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>\n\n        <span class=\"tok-com\"># Frame 1: Render &amp; locate widget rectangles</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.frame():\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>):\n                username = ctx.input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;user&quot;</span>, username, autofocus=<span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>)\n                <span class=\"tok-kw\">if</span> ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Sign In&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>):\n                    submitted = <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>\n                btn_id = ctx.last_id\n\n        btn_rect = ctx.get_rect(btn_id)\n\n        <span class=\"tok-com\"># Frame 2: Type UTF-8 text into focused input</span>\n        ctx.input_text(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;ada_lovelace&quot;</span>)\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.frame():\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>):\n                username = ctx.input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;user&quot;</span>, username)\n                ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Sign In&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>)\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">assert</span> username == <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;ada_lovelace&quot;</span>\n\n        <span class=\"tok-com\"># Frame 3 &amp; 4: Click the Sign In button (press + release)</span>\n        ctx.input_click(btn_rect.x + <span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>, btn_rect.y + <span class=\"tok-num\">10</span>)\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.frame():\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>):\n                username = ctx.input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;user&quot;</span>, username)\n                submitted |= ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Sign In&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>)\n        ctx.input_mouse_button(ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">MouseButton</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">LEFT</span>, <span class=\"tok-kw\">False</span>)\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.frame():\n            <span class=\"tok-kw\">with</span> ctx.column(pad=<span class=\"tok-num\">24</span>, gap=<span class=\"tok-num\">12</span>):\n                username = ctx.input(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;user&quot;</span>, username)\n                submitted |= ctx.button(<span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;Sign In&quot;</span>, variant=ui.<span class=\"tok-cls\">ButtonVariant</span>.<span class=\"tok-cls\">PRIMARY</span>)\n\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">assert</span> submitted is <span class=\"tok-kw\">True</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-kw\">assert</span> ctx.render_to_png(tmp_path / <span class=\"tok-str\">&quot;login_verified.png&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"3-custom-gpu-backends-customrenderer-drawdata\">3. Custom GPU Backends (<code>CustomRenderer</code> &amp; <code>DrawData</code>)</h2>\n<p>Want to render <code>nexa</code> inside your own <strong>Vulkan</strong>, <strong>Metal</strong>, <strong>Direct3D 12</strong>, **<code>wgpu</code><strong>, or </strong><code>moderngl</code>** swapchain?</p>\n<ol><li>Supply texture atlas callbacks via <code>ui.CustomRenderer(on_create=..., on_update=..., on_destroy=...)</code>.</li><li>Call <code>ctx.set_viewport(w, h, dpi_scale)</code>, inject OS events via <code>ctx.input_*</code>, and run <code>dd = ctx.end_frame()</code>.</li><li>Upload <code>dd.vertices_bytes()</code> (<code>64</code> bytes per <code>cui_vertex</code> SDF primitive) and <code>dd.indices_bytes()</code> (<code>uint32</code>), then iterate <code>for cmd in dd.commands():</code> (<code>clip</code>, <code>texture</code>, <code>index_offset</code>, <code>index_count</code>).</li></ol>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"4-minimal-stripped-builds-single-file-executables\">4. Minimal Stripped Builds &amp; Single-File Executables</h2>\n<p>Compile a stripped custom shared library removing unused subsystems via CLI or environment variables:</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>bash</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># Default full build (~652 KB: SW + GL 3.3 + OS Windowing + Embedded Fonts + PNG/JPEG)\npython3 -m nexa.build\n\n# Minimal LTO build with Software Renderer (~499 KB)\npython3 -m nexa.build --minimal --lto\n\n# Ultra-minimal Core-Only LTO build for custom GPU engines (~487 KB)\npython3 -m nexa.build --minimal --no-sw --lto</code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"freezing-with-pyinstaller-or-nuitka\">Freezing with PyInstaller or Nuitka</h3>\n<p><code>nexa</code> registers an automatic PyInstaller hook (<code>nexa._pyinstaller</code>) that bundles <code>libnexa_cui</code> and excludes build-time compiler helpers (<code>nexa.build</code>, <code>setuptools</code>, <code>distutils</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"code-panel\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span>bash</span><button class=\"copy-mini\" data-copy-code=\"1\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># PyInstaller single-file binary\npyinstaller --onefile $(python3 -c &quot;import nexa.build as b; print(&#x27; &#x27;.join(b.freeze_flags(&#x27;pyinstaller&#x27;)))&quot;) app.py\n\n# Nuitka standalone native compilation\npython3 -m nuitka --onefile $(python3 -c &quot;import nexa.build as b; print(&#x27; &#x27;.join(b.freeze_flags(&#x27;nuitka&#x27;)))&quot;) app.py</code></pre></div>", "toc": [{"title": "1. Custom Vector canvas & Persistent state_buffer", "id": "1-custom-vector-canvas-persistent-state-buffer"}, {"title": "2. Automated Headless UI Testing & PNG Snapshots", "id": "2-automated-headless-ui-testing-png-snapshots"}, {"title": "3. Custom GPU Backends (CustomRenderer & DrawData)", "id": "3-custom-gpu-backends-customrenderer-drawdata"}, {"title": "4. Minimal Stripped Builds & Single-File Executables", "id": "4-minimal-stripped-builds-single-file-executables"}]}], "search": [{"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "Getting Started & Core Mental Model", "anchor": "", "text": "Welcome to **nexa**! Whether you have built desktop UIs with Tkinter, PyQt, Dear ImGui, or React—or this is your very first Python GUI library—this guide walks you from zero to building fast, polished desktop tools in minutes."}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "1. Installation & Requirements", "anchor": "1-installation-requirements", "text": "Install nexa from the repository root:"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "What you need (and what you *don't* need)", "anchor": "what-you-need-and-what-you-don-t-need", "text": "**Python 3.9+** (zero third-party runtime Python packages—pure standard library). **Any C99 compiler** when installing from source (gcc or clang on Linux/macOS, MSVC cl or MinGW gcc on Windows). **No python3-dev headers, no CMake, and no li"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "2. Your First 15-Line Window", "anchor": "2-your-first-15-line-window", "text": "Create a file named first_app.py and run python3 first_app.py:"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "Headless Screenshot Mode (Servers, Containers & CI)", "anchor": "headless-screenshot-mode-servers-containers-ci", "text": "Don't have a display attached right now? Every nexa app can render pixel-identical frames off-screen and save a PNG screenshot via environment variables:"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "3. How nexa Thinks: Value-Returning Immediate Mode", "anchor": "3-how-nexa-thinks-value-returning-immediate-mode", "text": "Traditional retained-mode toolkits (Tkinter, Qt, GTK) force you to keep **two copies of your state** synchronized: Your Python data (user.name), and Hidden state inside widget objects (name_entry.setText(...), on_text_changed callbacks, sig"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "4. Widget Identity (id & id_scope)", "anchor": "4-widget-identity-id-id-scope", "text": "To animate hover states, track keyboard focus, and remember scroll offsets across frames, nexa hashes an ID string for every interactive widget: **Controls with a unique key parameter** (input(\"email\", ...), tabs(\"main_tabs\", ...), slider(\""}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "5. Unconditional vs. Conditional with Scopes", "anchor": "5-unconditional-vs-conditional-with-scopes", "text": "nexa uses Python with statements so you can never forget a *_end() call. There are two kinds of scopes:"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "A. Unconditional Layout Scopes (always render children)", "anchor": "a-unconditional-layout-scopes-always-render-children", "text": "Containers that always open and close cleanly: box, row, column, stack, grid, card, scroll, split id_scope, disabled_scope, clip_scope button_group, swipe_item, spotlight, dock, carousel, card_stack, kanban, virtual_list, reorder menu_bar, "}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "B. Conditional Scopes (check if scope: before rendering children!)", "anchor": "b-conditional-scopes-check-if-scope-before-rendering-children", "text": "Overlays, disclosures, menus, and popups only build their children when open or visible. Always bind as s: and check if s:: Overlays & Menus: dialog, sheet, popover, hover_card, menu, context_menu, user_menu, menu_bar_menu Disclosures & Tre"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "6. Inspecting Transitions (changed, submitted, focused, blurred) & Rects", "anchor": "6-inspecting-transitions-changed-submitted-focused-blurred-rects", "text": "Even though widgets return updated values directly, you often want to know *how* a widget transitioned on the current frame (for example, running a search when the user presses **Enter** inside ui.input): On an explicit ctx: ui.UI instance,"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "Widget Hit Rectangles (last_id, last_rect, get_rect)", "anchor": "widget-hit-rectangles-last-id-last-rect-get-rect", "text": "Because CUI computes flexbox/grid layout in a single pass inside end_frame(): During draw(), ctx.last_id gives the uint32 ID of the widget you just emitted, and ctx.last_rect returns its cached Rect(x, y, w, h) from the previous frame. Imme"}, {"slug": "getting-started", "chapter": "Getting Started", "heading": "Next Steps", "anchor": "next-steps", "text": "Choose the coding style you want to learn first (most developers read **both**, because they share the exact same widget names and compose together!): **[Functional & Procedural Tutorial →](tutorial-functional.md)** — Closures, explicit ctx"}, {"slug": "tutorial-functional", "chapter": "Functional & Procedural", "heading": "Tutorial: Functional & Procedural Coding", "anchor": "", "text": "nexa lets you write clean, Pythonic desktop applications **without a single class** when you want speed, simplicity, and direct data flow. In fact, nexa supports **two closely related non-OOP styles**: **Top-Level Functional Style** (import"}, {"slug": "tutorial-functional", "chapter": "Functional & Procedural", "heading": "Lesson 1: Top-Level Functional Basics", "anchor": "lesson-1-top-level-functional-basics", "text": "With ui.run(draw), your draw function takes **0 arguments** (or 1 ctx: ui.UI argument—ui.run inspects its signature automatically!). Wait—notice how clean nonlocal celsius is for 1–3 variables. What when you have 10+ state fields? In proced"}, {"slug": "tutorial-functional", "chapter": "Functional & Procedural", "heading": "Lesson 2: Mastering Flexbox, Sizing & Grids", "anchor": "lesson-2-mastering-flexbox-sizing-grids", "text": "Every container in nexa (box, row, column, stack, grid, card, scroll) uses the same single-pass constraint layout system."}, {"slug": "tutorial-functional", "chapter": "Functional & Procedural", "heading": "Lesson 3: Procedural Decomposition (Plain Functions + State Dict)", "anchor": "lesson-3-procedural-decomposition-plain-functions-state-dict", "text": "As a procedural app grows beyond ~100 lines, split your UI into plain functions that accept (ctx: ui.UI, state: dict). Notice how readable, modular, and testable this is—no inheritance required:"}, {"slug": "tutorial-functional", "chapter": "Functional & Procedural", "heading": "Lesson 4: Manual Frame Loop (while app.frame():)", "anchor": "lesson-4-manual-frame-loop-while-app-frame", "text": "app.run(draw) is simply a convenience loop around app.frame(). Whenever you want explicit per-frame control—for example, draining a network queue, stepping a physics simulation, or driving custom frame timing—write the while app.frame(): lo"}, {"slug": "tutorial-functional", "chapter": "Functional & Procedural", "heading": "Lesson 5: Complete Procedural Project — Expense & Budget Tracker", "anchor": "lesson-5-complete-procedural-project-expense-budget-tracker", "text": "Below is a complete, 100% standalone procedural application combining **split panes**, **forms & money input**, **keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+K command palette)**, **donut chart**, and **sortable table**:"}, {"slug": "tutorial-functional", "chapter": "Functional & Procedural", "heading": "Next Steps", "anchor": "next-steps", "text": "Ready to scale up to multi-screen applications with reusable custom components, routing history, and reactive stores? Continue to **[Object-Oriented (OOP) Architecture →](tutorial-oop.md)**."}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "chapter": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "heading": "Tutorial: Object-Oriented (OOP) Architecture", "anchor": "", "text": "When your application grows into multiple views, reusable widget cards, shared state stores, and background workers, nexa provides a clean, zero-boilerplate Object-Oriented layer built directly on top of its immediate-mode engine: **ui.Appl"}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "chapter": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "heading": "Functional/Procedural vs. OOP: Side-by-Side", "anchor": "functional-procedural-vs-oop-side-by-side", "text": "Both paradigms call the **exact same widget methods** and can even be mixed inside the same frame!"}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "chapter": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "heading": "Lesson 1: Subclassing ui.Application", "anchor": "lesson-1-subclassing-ui-application", "text": "You can configure window defaults either as **class attributes** or via **super().__init__(...)** arguments: You can also override __init__ and pass title, width, height, theme, accent directly to super().__init__(\"Custom Title\", width=720,"}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "chapter": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "heading": "Lesson 2: Reusable ui.Component & Automatic ID Isolation", "anchor": "lesson-2-reusable-ui-component-automatic-id-isolation", "text": "In raw immediate-mode UIs, rendering two components that both contain ctx.button(\"Increment\") would normally collide on the ID \"Increment\". ui.Component solves this automatically: calling my_component(ctx) (or my_component() inside a frame)"}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "chapter": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "heading": "Lesson 3: Multi-Screen Navigation with ui.View & ui.Router", "anchor": "lesson-3-multi-screen-navigation-with-ui-view-ui-router", "text": "Every ui.Application comes with self.router pre-wired to wake the window on navigation: **self.router.register(\"route_name\", MyView(...))** — Register a View instance (the first registered route becomes active automatically). **self.router."}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "chapter": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "heading": "Lesson 4: Reactive State with ui.Store[T]", "anchor": "lesson-4-reactive-state-with-ui-store-t", "text": "In multi-view OOP apps, passing raw dicts between 6 views can get messy. ui.Store[T] holds shared state, notifies subscribers on change, and automatically wakes the UI window when mutated: **Thread-safety tip:** When updating a `Store` from"}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "chapter": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "heading": "Lesson 5: Complete OOP Capstone — Incident Response Console", "anchor": "lesson-5-complete-oop-capstone-incident-response-console", "text": "Here is a complete, 100% standalone multi-view OOP application combining **Application**, **Store**, **Router**, **two View screens (OverviewView & DetailView)**, **reusable IncidentCard Components**, **live accent switching**, and **backgr"}, {"slug": "tutorial-oop", "chapter": "Object-Oriented (OOP)", "heading": "Next Steps", "anchor": "next-steps", "text": "Learn every detail of **Accents, Tones, OKLCH Color Tokens, Custom Fonts, and Icons** in **[Theming & Styling →](theming-and-styling.md)**. Add **async HTTP APIs, streaming LLMs, and multi-threaded workers** in **[Concurrency & Async →](con"}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "chapter": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "heading": "Theming, Accents, Tones, Colors & Typography", "anchor": "", "text": "nexa ships with a perceptually calibrated **OKLCH / OKLab** design system out of the box—complete with smooth Light/Dark cross-fading, **8 built-in Accent palettes**, **9 semantic Tones**, **34 live-editable Token slots**, embedded **Inter*"}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "chapter": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "heading": "1. Light & Dark Theme Modes (ui.ThemeMode)", "anchor": "1-light-dark-theme-modes-ui-thememode", "text": "Switch between Light and Dark modes at startup or dynamically at runtime (surfaces and text smoothly interpolate across frames):"}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "chapter": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "heading": "2. The 8 Built-In ui.Accent Palettes", "anchor": "2-the-8-built-in-ui-accent-palettes", "text": "ui.Accent defines **exactly 8 built-in primary highlight palettes** (matching CUI's cui_accent enum 0..7): **Important:** Only those 8 members exist on `ui.Accent` (`NEUTRAL`, `VIOLET`, `BLUE`, `GREEN`, `AMBER`, `ORANGE`, `CORAL`, `ROSE`). "}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "chapter": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "heading": "3. Semantic ui.Tones (Badges, Alerts, Toasts, Kanban, Gantt)", "anchor": "3-semantic-ui-tones-badges-alerts-toasts-kanban-gantt", "text": "While ui.Accent controls the *entire window's* primary highlight palette, **ui.Tone** colors individual status elements (badge, alert, banner, toast, CalEvent, GanttTask, SwipeAction, status_bar_text) so semantic meanings stay consistent re"}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "chapter": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "heading": "4. Custom Brand Colors, Live Token Overrides & Perceptual OKLCH", "anchor": "4-custom-brand-colors-live-token-overrides-perceptual-oklch", "text": "Every color in nexa can be passed as: A **ui.Color(r, g, b, a=255)** value A hex string: **\"#10b981\"** or **ui.Color.hex(\"#10b981\")** (6-digit #RRGGBB or 8-digit #RRGGBBAA) An RGB/RGBA tuple: **(16, 185, 129)** or **(16, 185, 129, 200)** A "}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "chapter": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "heading": "All 34 ui.Token Slots", "anchor": "all-34-ui-token-slots", "text": "**Surfaces**: BACKGROUND, SURFACE, SURFACE_RAISED, SURFACE_MUTED **Text**: FOREGROUND, TEXT_SECONDARY, TEXT_MUTED **Borders**: BORDER, BORDER_SUBTLE, BORDER_STRONG **Accent**: ACCENT, ACCENT_STRONG, ACCENT_SUBTLE, ACCENT_FOREGROUND **Semant"}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "chapter": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "heading": "5. Typography, Custom .ttf Fonts & International Fallback", "anchor": "5-typography-custom-ttf-fonts-international-fallback", "text": "Out of the box, nexa embeds: **Inter** (FontRole.BODY, FontRole.MEDIUM, FontRole.DISPLAY) **Geist Mono** (FontRole.MONO) **Lucide** (FontRole.ICONS — 168 crisp vector icons) To load your own .ttf / .otf typeface or add CJK / Arabic / Persia"}, {"slug": "theming-and-styling", "chapter": "Theming, Accents & Icons", "heading": "6. Icons (ui.Icon)", "anchor": "6-icons-ui-icon", "text": "All **168 bundled Lucide icons** are UTF-8 string constants on ui.Icon and can be passed to icon=, ui.icon(...), ui.icon_button(...), ui.nav_item(...), or looked up dynamically by name: Popular icons include: **Navigation & Arrows**: ARROW_"}, {"slug": "concurrency-and-async", "chapter": "Concurrency & Asyncio", "heading": "Concurrency, Multithreading, asyncio, & Networking", "anchor": "", "text": "Desktop GUIs freeze the moment you run a slow HTTP request, SQLite query, or LLM stream on the UI thread. nexa is engineered from the C99 layer up for responsive, zero-CPU-idle concurrency: **Every native C call releases Python's GIL**, so "}, {"slug": "concurrency-and-async", "chapter": "Concurrency & Asyncio", "heading": "Pattern 1: BackgroundRunner (Threads, Streaming & HTTP JSON)", "anchor": "pattern-1-backgroundrunner-threads-streaming-http-json", "text": "ui.BackgroundRunner.for_app(app) (or self.runner inside any OOP ui.Application) manages a bounded pool of daemon threads and delivers on_done, on_item, and on_error callbacks **on the UI thread**, waking the window automatically."}, {"slug": "concurrency-and-async", "chapter": "Concurrency & Asyncio", "heading": "Built-in Zero-Dependency HTTP Helpers (fetch_json & fetch_bytes)", "anchor": "built-in-zero-dependency-http-helpers-fetch-json-fetch-bytes", "text": "Need to call a REST API without pulling in third-party packages? BackgroundRunner includes stdlib urllib-backed fetch_json and fetch_bytes:"}, {"slug": "concurrency-and-async", "chapter": "Concurrency & Asyncio", "heading": "Pattern 2: Producer-Consumer Channel[T] & Thread-Safe LogBuffer", "anchor": "pattern-2-producer-consumer-channel-t-thread-safe-logbuffer", "text": "When a long-lived background thread (e.g., a WebSocket listener, serial port reader, or file watcher) emits high-frequency events: **ui.Channel(maxsize=256, wake=app.wake)**: Thread-safe MPSC queue. Background threads call channel.send(item"}, {"slug": "concurrency-and-async", "chapter": "Concurrency & Asyncio", "heading": "Pattern 3: Cooperative Single-Thread asyncio (await app.run_async(...))", "anchor": "pattern-3-cooperative-single-thread-asyncio-await-app-run-async", "text": "Already using httpx.AsyncClient, aiohttp, websockets, or asyncio.StreamReader? Run nexa **cooperatively inside your existing asyncio event loop**—zero extra threads, zero locks! OOP ui.Application subclasses also support await MyApp().run_a"}, {"slug": "concurrency-and-async", "chapter": "Concurrency & Asyncio", "heading": "Pattern 4: Dedicated-Thread AsyncBridge", "anchor": "pattern-4-dedicated-thread-asyncbridge", "text": "If your main thread runs synchronous app.run(draw) (ensuring the OS window loop never waits on a slow coroutine) while third-party async def coroutines or async generators run on a dedicated background asyncio event loop thread, use nexa.ai"}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "Complete Component Reference (150+ Widgets Across 19 Domains)", "anchor": "", "text": "Every widget method below is available **both** on ctx: ui.UI (ctx.button(...)) **and** as a top-level function when inside an active frame (import nexa as ui; ui.button(...))."}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "1. Layout & Containers (nexa.widgets.layout)", "anchor": "1-layout-containers-nexa-widgets-layout", "text": "All layout scopes are **unconditional** (with ui.row(...): always enters). **box(*, id=None, dir=Direction.COLUMN, width=None, height=None, min_width=0, max_width=0, min_height=0, max_height=0, pad=0, pad_x=0, pad_y=0, pad_top=0, pad_right="}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "2. Text & Typography (nexa.widgets.text)", "anchor": "2-text-typography-nexa-widgets-text", "text": "**text(content, *, font=FontRole.BODY, size=0, color=None, align=TextAlign.LEFT, max_lines=0, selectable=False, strikethrough=False, underline=False, nowrap=False, width=None)** **heading(content, level=2)** (level in 1..4) **label(content)"}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "3. Buttons & Actions (nexa.widgets.actions)", "anchor": "3-buttons-actions-nexa-widgets-actions", "text": "**button(label, *, variant=ButtonVariant.DEFAULT, size=ControlSize.MD, icon=None, icon_right=None, disabled=False, loading=False, full_width=False, selected=False, tooltip=None, shortcut=None, width=None, color=None) -> bool** ButtonVariant"}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "4. Selection Controls (nexa.widgets.selection)", "anchor": "4-selection-controls-nexa-widgets-selection", "text": "**checkbox(label, checked: bool, *, description=None, indeterminate=False, disabled=False) -> bool** **switch(label, on: bool, *, description=None, disabled=False) -> bool** **radio(label, current: int, option_value: int) -> int** **radio_g"}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "5. Text & Specialized Inputs (nexa.widgets.inputs)", "anchor": "5-text-specialized-inputs-nexa-widgets-inputs", "text": "**input(id, value: str, *, max_bytes=512, label=None, placeholder=None, icon=None, hint=None, error=None, password=False, disabled=False, clearable=False, autofocus=False, read_only=False, size=ControlSize.MD, width=None, prefix=None, suffi"}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "6. Pickers (nexa.widgets.pickers)", "anchor": "6-pickers-nexa-widgets-pickers", "text": "**select(id, options, selected: int, *, label=None, placeholder=None, width=None, size=ControlSize.MD) -> int** **combobox(id, options, selected: int, *, label=None, placeholder=\"Search...\", width=None) -> int** **multi_select(id, options, "}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "7. Navigation (nexa.widgets.navigation)", "anchor": "7-navigation-nexa-widgets-navigation", "text": "**tabs(id, labels, selected: int, *, variant=TabsVariant.LINE, icons=None, badges=None) -> int** (TabsVariant: LINE, PILL, ENCLOSED) **nav_section(title)** | **nav_item(label, *, icon=None, badge=None, selected=False, disabled=False, group="}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "8. Overlays, Menus & Disclosure (nexa.widgets.overlays)", "anchor": "8-overlays-menus-disclosure-nexa-widgets-overlays", "text": "All popup/overlay scopes are **conditional**—always write with ui.dialog(...) as d: if d: ...! **tooltip(text)** — Attaches a hover tooltip to the immediately preceding widget. **popover(id, *, place=Placement.BOTTOM_START, width=0)** (popo"}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "9. Feedback, Status & Badges (nexa.widgets.feedback)", "anchor": "9-feedback-status-badges-nexa-widgets-feedback", "text": "**toast(title, *, description=None, tone=Tone.NEUTRAL, duration=4.0, action=None, dismissible=True) -> int** (+ toast_action_clicked(h), toast_dismiss(h)) **alert(title, *, description=None, tone=Tone.INFO, icon=None, action=None, dismissib"}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "10. Data, Virtual Lists, Tables, Grids & Code (nexa.widgets.data)", "anchor": "10-data-virtual-lists-tables-grids-code-nexa-widgets-data", "text": "**tree(label, expanded=False, *, icon=None, badge=None, leaf=False, selected=False)** -> TreeScope (if tr: for children; tr.expanded, tr.clicked). **list_item(title, *, subtitle=None, trailing=None, icon=None, avatar=None, badge=None, badge"}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "11. Charts & Data Visualization (nexa.widgets.charts)", "anchor": "11-charts-data-visualization-nexa-widgets-charts", "text": "**line_chart(id, series: Sequence[Series], *, labels=None, height=200.0, width=None, smooth=False, area=False, show_points=False, show_grid=True, show_legend=False, y_min=0, y_max=0, reference_y=None, reference_label=None, y_format=None)** "}, {"slug": "components-reference", "chapter": "150+ Components Reference", "heading": "12–19. Planning, AI, Social, Media, Motion, Chrome, Tools & Node/Canvas", "anchor": "12-19-planning-ai-social-media-motion-chrome-tools-node-canvas", "text": "**Planning (nexa.widgets.planning)**: kanban(id) -> KanbanScope (board.column(title, count, dot=..., width=...), board.card(id), board.move) week_calendar(id, week_start: Date, events: Sequence[CalEvent], **opts) -> tuple[list[CalEvent], in"}, {"slug": "advanced-rendering-and-packaging", "chapter": "Canvas, GPU & Packaging", "heading": "Custom Canvas, Headless Testing, Custom GPU & Packaging", "anchor": "", "text": "Beyond its 150+ built-in components, nexa exposes every low-level primitive of the underlying C99 engine so you can build custom vector instruments, write deterministic CI tests, plug into Vulkan/Metal/Direct3D/wgpu, or ship tiny standalone"}, {"slug": "advanced-rendering-and-packaging", "chapter": "Canvas, GPU & Packaging", "heading": "1. Custom Vector canvas & Persistent state_buffer", "anchor": "1-custom-vector-canvas-persistent-state-buffer", "text": "Reserve layout space with ctx.canvas(id, width, height, paint_fn)—nexa runs flexbox layout first, then invokes paint_fn(ctx, rect) with the resolved screen Rect(x, y, w, h) and returns a CanvasResult (rect, mouse, hovered, pressed, clicked)"}, {"slug": "advanced-rendering-and-packaging", "chapter": "Canvas, GPU & Packaging", "heading": "2. Automated Headless UI Testing & PNG Snapshots", "anchor": "2-automated-headless-ui-testing-png-snapshots", "text": "You can test **every click, keystroke, text edit, and file drop** in pytest at thousands of frames per second without opening an OS window:"}, {"slug": "advanced-rendering-and-packaging", "chapter": "Canvas, GPU & Packaging", "heading": "3. Custom GPU Backends (CustomRenderer & DrawData)", "anchor": "3-custom-gpu-backends-customrenderer-drawdata", "text": "Want to render nexa inside your own **Vulkan**, **Metal**, **Direct3D 12**, **wgpu**, or **moderngl** swapchain? Supply texture atlas callbacks via ui.CustomRenderer(on_create=..., on_update=..., on_destroy=...). Call ctx.set_viewport(w, h,"}, {"slug": "advanced-rendering-and-packaging", "chapter": "Canvas, GPU & Packaging", "heading": "4. Minimal Stripped Builds & Single-File Executables", "anchor": "4-minimal-stripped-builds-single-file-executables", "text": "Compile a stripped custom shared library removing unused subsystems via CLI or environment variables:"}, {"slug": "advanced-rendering-and-packaging", "chapter": "Canvas, GPU & Packaging", "heading": "Freezing with PyInstaller or Nuitka", "anchor": "freezing-with-pyinstaller-or-nuitka", "text": "nexa registers an automatic PyInstaller hook (nexa._pyinstaller) that bundles libnexa_cui and excludes build-time compiler helpers (nexa.build, setuptools, distutils):"}]};
